{"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit?scriptVersionId=353830907\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7962d3f8","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"686e3b2d-c3d7-477d-bfa1-204e9038e9f8","_uuid":"f4758bb9-730b-475a-86da-fc63aafc5769","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.012608,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.083038+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.07043+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# IEEE-CIS EDA and Leakage Audit — Kaggle-Modular Thesis Edition\n","\n","**Refined from:** Kaggle kernel `iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit` (version 3).\n","The source notebook is preserved unchanged; this is a separate artifact.\n","\n","## Notebook architecture\n","\n","This file intentionally remains a single Kaggle notebook script with the original\n","15-section thesis narrative. Modularity is achieved inside the notebook by keeping\n","each section in three layers where applicable: reusable definitions, a small\n","orchestration block, and presentation/export code. Public helper interfaces are\n","preserved unless a correctness fix requires an explicit new argument.\n","\n","The design goal is a restart-and-run-all artifact that is readable in Kaggle, while\n","still allowing the statistical, leakage, decision and export components to be\n","tested independently.\n","\n","## Research questions\n","\n","This notebook produces evidence for seven questions, and nothing else:\n","\n","| # | Question | Sections |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| RQ1 | **Leakage risk** — can any development decision be traced to out-of-time data? | 3, 15 |\n","| RQ2 | **Temporal feature validity** — which features change distribution across the development period? | 5, 10 |\n","| RQ3 | **Distribution drift** — how large is the shift, on a stated scale, with stated sample sizes? | 5 |\n","| RQ4 | **Missingness stability** — is \"this field is blank\" a stable signal, or a product-mix artefact? | 6 |\n","| RQ5 | **Redundant feature stability** — do the V-series redundancy groups reproduce across blocks? | 7 |\n","| RQ6 | **Graph-entity readiness** — what coverage, persistence and cold-start exposure do the candidate entity columns carry? | 8 |\n","| RQ7 | **OOT generalization risk** — what is known about the holdout *without* letting it influence any decision? | 3, 8, 12 |\n","\n","## Scope: exploratory versus confirmatory\n","\n","Everything in this notebook is **exploratory and descriptive**. No hypothesis was\n","pre-registered before the data were seen, no model is fitted, and no effect is\n","estimated under an identification strategy. Consequently:\n","\n","* p-values here are **screening devices with a multiplicity correction**, not\n","  confirmatory tests. A Benjamini–Hochberg-adjusted p-value below 0.05 licenses\n","  \"worth a closer look\", not \"established\".\n","* PSI, KS and lift figures are **descriptive statistics with configured decision\n","  bands**. The bands are choices about review capacity, stated in Section 1 and\n","  snapshotted into every exported decision.\n","* Every association reported is **predictive, not causal**. No claim of the form\n","  \"X causes fraud\" is made or supported anywhere in this notebook.\n","* The one **confirmatory-style** element is the leakage protocol itself: the\n","  quarantine assertions in Section 3 are pass/fail invariants, not exploratory\n","  findings, and a failure stops the run.\n","\n","## What changed relative to the source notebook\n","\n","| Source notebook | This notebook |\n","|---|---|\n","| `DRIFT_CORR = 0.30` on Pearson correlation, unsourced | Spearman throughout; the threshold's empirical distribution is shown and a quantile-derived alternative computed (Section 10) |\n","| Drift judged by one correlation | PSI (dev-learned bin edges) + KS with BH correction + per-block lift stability, combined (Section 5) |\n","| Missingness patterns tested in aggregate | Same pattern-collapsing, plus ProductCD stratification and an explicit Simpson-type reversal check (Section 6) |\n","| V-series grouped once on a dev sample, Pearson, union-find | Per-block Spearman hierarchical clustering, cross-block stability, MI-based representative with deterministic tie-breaking (Section 7) |\n","| Entities described qualitatively | Coverage, cardinality, persistence, degree bands, and OOT cold-start on two explicit denominators (Section 8) |\n","| Fixed 5-block split | The same diagnostics repeated at 4, 5, 6 and 8 blocks with verdict-change tracking (Section 9) |\n","| `feature_decisions.csv` | `feature_risk_table.csv`, `decisions_ledger.json`, `run_manifest.json`, `entity_cold_start_summary.csv`, `block_sensitivity_summary.csv` |\n","| Leakage protocol stated in prose | Registered fitted objects, executable quarantine assertions and a reusable `LeakageAuditor` (Sections 3, 15) |\n","| `warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")` | Warnings left enabled; failures are logged with their fallback, never swallowed |"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2781f1ff","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"5b252395-4b70-4937-aec7-4f2de914de56","_uuid":"d2d4ba2b-b558-4734-8084-6c18f46a89f6","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.00975,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.102638+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.092888+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Environment and Reproducibility\n","\n","Three cells: dependency check, the single configuration dictionary, and the\n","environment/hashing utilities. Nothing below Section 1 hard-codes a threshold —\n","every one is read from `CONFIG`, and `CONFIG` is snapshotted into every exported\n","decision so a result can always be traced back to the rules that produced it."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"31776fb2","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"b95f3a52-fb99-455d-b91c-27d2c5ae6fe4","_uuid":"21bb7f96-2448-4605-88ad-4cb42d09c7c2","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.125269Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.124899Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.003782Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.002664Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":2.892353,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.005863+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:49.11351+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:11:51 | INFO    | Imports complete.\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["   package required_min installed  available  compatible\n","matplotlib          3.5    3.10.0       True        True\n","     numpy         1.23     2.0.2       True        True\n","    pandas          1.5     2.3.3       True        True\n","     scipy          1.9    1.16.3       True        True\n","   sklearn          1.1     1.6.1       True        True\n"]}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 1a - imports and dependency check.\"\"\"\n","\n","from __future__ import annotations\n","\n","import gc\n","import hashlib\n","import importlib\n","import json\n","import logging\n","import os\n","import platform\n","import sys\n","import warnings\n","from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","from typing import Any, Callable, Dict, Iterable, List, Mapping, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\n","from packaging.version import InvalidVersion, Version\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Warnings are NOT suppressed globally. Relevant warnings are addressed or\n","# documented in-line. Only this one noisy, understood case is narrowed.\n","warnings.simplefilter(\"default\")\n","\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\n","\"ignore\",\n","category=DeprecationWarning,\n","message=r\"datetime\\.datetime\\.utcnow\\(\\) is deprecated.*\",\n",")\n","\n","REQUIRED_PACKAGES = {\n","    \"numpy\": \"1.23\",\n","    \"pandas\": \"1.5\",\n","    \"scipy\": \"1.9\",\n","    \"sklearn\": \"1.1\",\n","    \"matplotlib\": \"3.5\",\n","}\n","\n","\n","def check_dependencies(required: Mapping[str, str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Validate imports and minimum package versions.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        required: Mapping of importable module name to minimum supported version.\n","\n","    Returns:\n","        A dataframe containing the installed version and compatibility result.\n","\n","    Raises:\n","        ImportError: If a package is missing.\n","        RuntimeError: If a package is older than the configured minimum or its\n","            version cannot be interpreted safely.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n","    missing: List[str] = []\n","    incompatible: List[str] = []\n","\n","    for name, minimum in sorted(required.items()):\n","        try:\n","            module = importlib.import_module(name)\n","        except ImportError:\n","            missing.append(name)\n","            rows.append({\n","                \"package\": name,\n","                \"required_min\": minimum,\n","                \"installed\": None,\n","                \"available\": False,\n","                \"compatible\": False,\n","            })\n","            continue\n","\n","        installed = getattr(module, \"__version__\", None)\n","        compatible = False\n","        try:\n","            compatible = installed is not None and Version(installed) >= Version(minimum)\n","        except InvalidVersion:\n","            incompatible.append(f\"{name}>={minimum} required; found unparseable {installed!r}\")\n","        else:\n","            if not compatible:\n","                incompatible.append(f\"{name}>={minimum} required; found {installed or 'unknown'}\")\n","\n","        rows.append({\n","            \"package\": name,\n","            \"required_min\": minimum,\n","            \"installed\": installed,\n","            \"available\": True,\n","            \"compatible\": compatible,\n","        })\n","\n","    report = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","    if missing:\n","        raise ImportError(\n","            \"Missing required packages: \" + \", \".join(missing)\n","            + \". Install them before running this notebook; this notebook does \"\n","              \"not install packages itself.\"\n","        )\n","    if incompatible:\n","        raise RuntimeError(\"Incompatible package versions: \" + \"; \".join(incompatible))\n","    return report\n","\n","DEPENDENCY_REPORT = check_dependencies(REQUIRED_PACKAGES)\n","\n","from scipy import stats\n","from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import fcluster, linkage\n","from scipy.spatial.distance import squareform\n","from sklearn.feature_selection import mutual_info_classif\n","\n","plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\": 110, \"axes.grid\": True, \"grid.alpha\": 0.3})\n","\n","logging.basicConfig(\n","    level=logging.INFO,\n","    format=\"%(asctime)s | %(levelname)-7s | %(message)s\",\n","    datefmt=\"%H:%M:%S\",\n","    force=True,\n",")\n","LOG = logging.getLogger(\"leakage_audit\")\n","LOG.info(\"Imports complete.\")\n","print(DEPENDENCY_REPORT.to_string(index=False))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"44171328","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"72ea152d-c79a-404a-9d3f-a3c5844fc240","_uuid":"c1e6c2de-6aaa-4dfe-83cc-886bf629c897","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.027817Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.02738Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.040168Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.038892Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.025824,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.042089+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.016265+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["{\n","  \"RANDOM_SEED\": 42,\n","  \"TIME_COLUMN\": \"TransactionDT\",\n","  \"TARGET_COLUMN\": \"isFraud\",\n","  \"ID_COLUMN\": \"TransactionID\",\n","  \"N_BLOCKS\": 5,\n","  \"OOT_BLOCK\": 5,\n","  \"SECONDS_PER_DAY\": 86400,\n","  \"PSI_BINS\": 10,\n","  \"PSI_EPSILON\": 1e-06,\n","  \"PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD\": 0.1,\n","  \"PSI_SEVERE_THRESHOLD\": 0.25,\n","  \"KS_ALPHA\": 0.05,\n","  \"MULTIPLICITY_METHOD\": \"benjamini_hochberg\",\n","  \"TEMPORAL_CORRELATION_METHOD\": \"spearman\",\n","  \"SPEARMAN_RISK_THRESHOLD\": 0.3,\n","  \"CLUSTER_DISTANCE_THRESHOLD\": 0.1,\n","  \"CLUSTER_STABILITY_THRESHOLD\": 0.75,\n","  \"CORR_SAMPLE_ROWS\": 60000,\n","  \"V_MAX_MISSING_PCT\": 90.0,\n","  \"TOP_DECILE_QUANTILE\": 0.9,\n","  \"MIN_POSITIVES_FOR_LIFT\": 30,\n","  \"LIFT_STABILITY_MIN_BLOCKS\": 3,\n","  \"LIFT_STABILITY_THRESHOLD\": 0.75,\n","  \"FIXED_FPR\": 0.001,\n","  \"MIN_GROUP_N\": 500,\n","  \"MIN_ABS_DELTA_PP\": 0.25,\n","  \"MIN_NON_MISSING\": 1000,\n","  \"MIN_BLOCK_GROUP_N\": 50,\n","  \"PARTIAL_MISSING_MIN_RATE\": 0.001,\n","  \"PARTIAL_MISSING_MAX_RATE\": 0.999,\n","  \"ENTITY_COLD_START_MODERATE_THRESHOLD\": 0.05,\n","  \"ENTITY_COLD_START_HIGH_THRESHOLD\": 0.2,\n","  \"SENSITIVITY_BLOCK_COUNTS\": [\n","    4,\n","    5,\n","    6,\n","    8\n","  ],\n","  \"OUTPUT_DIRECTORY\": \"./artifacts\",\n","  \"SOURCE_NOTEBOOK_REF\": \"kaggle kernel iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit (version 3)\",\n","  \"CODE_VERSION\": \"thesis-refined-1.1.0\",\n","  \"SCRIPT_FILE_PATH\": null\n","}\n"]}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 1b - single configuration object.\n","\n","Every threshold in this notebook is a *configured decision rule*, not a law of\n","nature. Changing a value here changes every downstream verdict, and the value\n","used is snapshotted into run_manifest.json and decisions_ledger.json.\n","\"\"\"\n","\n","CONFIG: Dict[str, Any] = {\n","    # --- reproducibility -----------------------------------------------------\n","    \"RANDOM_SEED\": 42,\n","    # --- schema --------------------------------------------------------------\n","    \"TIME_COLUMN\": \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"TARGET_COLUMN\": \"isFraud\",\n","    \"ID_COLUMN\": \"TransactionID\",\n","    # --- temporal protocol ---------------------------------------------------\n","    \"N_BLOCKS\": 5,\n","    \"OOT_BLOCK\": 5,          # final chronological block is the OOT holdout\n","    \"SECONDS_PER_DAY\": 86_400,\n","    # --- drift diagnostics ---------------------------------------------------\n","    \"PSI_BINS\": 10,\n","    \"PSI_EPSILON\": 1e-6,     # documented floor for zero proportions\n","    \"PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD\": 0.10,\n","    \"PSI_SEVERE_THRESHOLD\": 0.25,\n","    \"KS_ALPHA\": 0.05,\n","    \"MULTIPLICITY_METHOD\": \"benjamini_hochberg\",\n","    \"TEMPORAL_CORRELATION_METHOD\": \"spearman\",\n","    \"SPEARMAN_RISK_THRESHOLD\": 0.30,   # retained but re-derived in Section 10\n","    # --- redundancy ----------------------------------------------------------\n","    \"CLUSTER_DISTANCE_THRESHOLD\": 0.10,   # distance = 1 - |Spearman|\n","    \"CLUSTER_STABILITY_THRESHOLD\": 0.75,  # share of dev block pairs agreeing\n","    \"CORR_SAMPLE_ROWS\": 60_000,\n","    \"V_MAX_MISSING_PCT\": 90.0,\n","    # --- lift ----------------------------------------------------------------\n","    \"TOP_DECILE_QUANTILE\": 0.90,\n","    \"MIN_POSITIVES_FOR_LIFT\": 30,\n","    \"LIFT_STABILITY_MIN_BLOCKS\": 3,\n","    \"LIFT_STABILITY_THRESHOLD\": 0.75,\n","    # --- evaluation ----------------------------------------------------------\n","    \"FIXED_FPR\": 0.001,\n","    # --- statistical guards --------------------------------------------------\n","    \"MIN_GROUP_N\": 500,\n","    \"MIN_ABS_DELTA_PP\": 0.25,\n","    \"MIN_NON_MISSING\": 1_000,\n","    \"MIN_BLOCK_GROUP_N\": 50,\n","    \"PARTIAL_MISSING_MIN_RATE\": 0.001,\n","    \"PARTIAL_MISSING_MAX_RATE\": 0.999,\n","    \"ENTITY_COLD_START_MODERATE_THRESHOLD\": 0.05,\n","    \"ENTITY_COLD_START_HIGH_THRESHOLD\": 0.20,\n","    # --- sensitivity ---------------------------------------------------------\n","    \"SENSITIVITY_BLOCK_COUNTS\": [4, 5, 6, 8],\n","    # --- io ------------------------------------------------------------------\n","    \"OUTPUT_DIRECTORY\": \"./artifacts\",\n","    \"SOURCE_NOTEBOOK_REF\": \"kaggle kernel iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit (version 3)\",\n","    \"CODE_VERSION\": \"thesis-refined-1.1.0\",\n","    \"SCRIPT_FILE_PATH\": None,  # optional explicit path when __file__ is unavailable\n","}\n","\n","RANDOM_SEED = CONFIG[\"RANDOM_SEED\"]\n","TIME_COLUMN = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]\n","TARGET_COLUMN = CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]\n","ID_COLUMN = CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]\n","N_BLOCKS = CONFIG[\"N_BLOCKS\"]\n","OOT_BLOCK = CONFIG[\"OOT_BLOCK\"]\n","DEV_BLOCKS = list(range(1, OOT_BLOCK))\n","OUTPUT_DIRECTORY = CONFIG[\"OUTPUT_DIRECTORY\"]\n","\n","np.random.seed(RANDOM_SEED)\n","os.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIRECTORY, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","print(json.dumps(CONFIG, indent=2, default=str))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"4f38b193","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"c9c6e6e4-4c0e-48d6-8902-852d3f8b5995","_uuid":"29c5fe86-000c-46aa-86a9-549335692116","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.064604Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.063586Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.079322Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.078254Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.028729,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.081046+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.052317+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["{\n","  \"executed_at_utc\": \"2026-09-29T09:11:52+00:00\",\n","  \"python\": \"3.12.13\",\n","  \"platform\": \"Linux-6.12.90+-x86_64-with-glibc2.35\",\n","  \"processor\": \"x86_64\",\n","  \"numpy\": \"2.0.2\",\n","  \"pandas\": \"2.3.3\",\n","  \"matplotlib\": \"3.10.0\",\n","  \"source_notebook\": \"kaggle kernel iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit (version 3)\",\n","  \"code_version\": \"thesis-refined-1.1.0\",\n","  \"random_seed\": 42,\n","  \"scipy\": \"1.16.3\",\n","  \"sklearn\": \"1.6.1\"\n","}\n"]}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 1c - environment capture and deterministic hashing.\"\"\"\n","\n","\n","def compute_dataframe_hash(\n","    frame: pd.DataFrame,\n","    columns: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None,\n","    sort_by: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None,\n",") -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"Return a SHA-256 fingerprint of stable dataframe content.\n","\n","    What is hashed, precisely: the row-wise pandas hash of the selected columns\n","    after deterministic sorting, concatenated in row order, plus the ordered\n","    column-name list and the row count. Values are hashed through\n","    ``pandas.util.hash_pandas_object``, so NaN positions and dtypes-as-values\n","    are included but float formatting is not. Nothing about file paths, machine\n","    or run time enters the hash - the same data yields the same hash anywhere.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        frame: dataframe to fingerprint.\n","        columns: subset of columns to hash (default: all, in sorted name order).\n","        sort_by: columns to sort by before hashing (default: no re-sort).\n","\n","    Returns:\n","        dict with keys sha256, n_rows, n_columns, columns_hashed, description.\n","\n","    Raises:\n","        TypeError: if ``frame`` is not a DataFrame.\n","        KeyError: if a requested column is absent.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if not isinstance(frame, pd.DataFrame):\n","        raise TypeError(\"compute_dataframe_hash expects a pandas DataFrame.\")\n","    cols = list(columns) if columns is not None else sorted(map(str, frame.columns))\n","    missing = [c for c in cols if c not in frame.columns]\n","    if missing:\n","        raise KeyError(f\"Cannot hash absent columns: {missing}\")\n","\n","    work = frame[cols]\n","    if sort_by:\n","        missing_sort = [c for c in sort_by if c not in frame.columns]\n","        if missing_sort:\n","            raise KeyError(f\"Cannot sort on absent columns: {missing_sort}\")\n","        work = work.assign(**{c: frame[c] for c in sort_by if c not in cols})\n","        work = work.sort_values(list(sort_by), kind=\"mergesort\")[cols]\n","\n","    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n","    digest.update((\"|\".join(cols)).encode(\"utf-8\"))\n","    digest.update(str(len(work)).encode(\"utf-8\"))\n","    chunk = 200_000\n","    for start in range(0, len(work), chunk):\n","        part = pd.util.hash_pandas_object(work.iloc[start:start + chunk], index=False)\n","        digest.update(np.asarray(part, dtype=np.uint64).tobytes())\n","    return {\n","        \"sha256\": digest.hexdigest(),\n","        \"n_rows\": int(len(work)),\n","        \"n_columns\": len(cols),\n","        \"columns_hashed\": cols if len(cols) <= 25 else cols[:25] + [\"...\"],\n","        \"description\": (\n","            \"SHA-256 over pandas row hashes of the listed columns (deterministic \"\n","            \"sort applied), the ordered column names and the row count.\"\n","        ),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def hash_file(path: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"SHA-256 of a file's raw bytes, with its size. Used for input inventory.\"\"\"\n","    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n","    size = 0\n","    with open(path, \"rb\") as handle:\n","        for block in iter(lambda: handle.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n","            digest.update(block)\n","            size += len(block)\n","    return {\"file\": os.path.basename(path), \"bytes\": size, \"sha256\": digest.hexdigest()}\n","\n","\n","RUN_ENVIRONMENT: Dict[str, Any] = {\n","    \"executed_at_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"),\n","    \"python\": sys.version.split()[0],\n","    \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n","    \"processor\": platform.machine(),\n","    \"numpy\": np.__version__,\n","    \"pandas\": pd.__version__,\n","    \"matplotlib\": matplotlib.__version__,\n","    \"source_notebook\": CONFIG[\"SOURCE_NOTEBOOK_REF\"],\n","    \"code_version\": CONFIG[\"CODE_VERSION\"],\n","    \"random_seed\": RANDOM_SEED,\n","}\n","for _pkg in (\"scipy\", \"sklearn\"):\n","    RUN_ENVIRONMENT[_pkg] = importlib.import_module(_pkg).__version__\n","\n","print(json.dumps(RUN_ENVIRONMENT, indent=2))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bcbdf11a","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"9bb52689-4952-47d0-8bc9-b73815b3cb90","_uuid":"e7b0a060-69a6-4ef3-a433-fedb7c6a34c4","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.009889,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.101017+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.091128+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Interpreting Section 1\n","\n","The seed is set once and passed explicitly to every function that consumes\n","randomness (mutual-information estimation is the only one). Sampling elsewhere is\n","*evenly spaced*, not random, so it is deterministic without needing a seed at\n","all and preserves chronology within whatever window it samples.\n","\n","`compute_dataframe_hash` states exactly what it hashes: pandas row hashes of the\n","named columns after a declared sort, plus the ordered column names and the row\n","count. It deliberately excludes file paths, machine identity and run time, so the\n","same data yields the same hash on Kaggle and on a laptop."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5e22804a","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"7fa89dd0-41b5-46c5-902e-a7754711c142","_uuid":"de08af5a-33e2-4509-8292-fabfa4048c7f","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.009759,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.120838+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.111079+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 2. Data Loading and Schema Validation\n","\n","Required columns are fatal if absent; optional entity columns are recorded as\n","omissions and the dependent analyses are marked *not computed* rather than\n","silently skipped. The identity table is a **left** join: 75% of transactions\n","having no identity record is the documented shape of this dataset, not a bug."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"4423262b","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"86e3e422-669f-4aa8-8f60-f57c49da36ef","_uuid":"f4209a29-b9ef-4887-b5dc-8517386be454","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.150917Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.150266Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.70601Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.705155Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":31.588196,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.719276+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:11:52.13108+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:11:52 | INFO    | Reading IEEE-CIS data from /kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection\n","09:12:23 | INFO    | Memory 1955 MB -> 1045 MB (47% saved)\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["{\n","  \"rows\": 590540,\n","  \"columns\": 434,\n","  \"identity_table_available\": true,\n","  \"n_identity_columns\": 40,\n","  \"n_d_series\": 15,\n","  \"n_v_series\": 339,\n","  \"entity_columns_available\": [\n","    \"card1\",\n","    \"card2\",\n","    \"card3\",\n","    \"card4\",\n","    \"card5\",\n","    \"card6\",\n","    \"addr1\",\n","    \"addr2\",\n","    \"P_emaildomain\",\n","    \"R_emaildomain\",\n","    \"DeviceInfo\",\n","    \"DeviceType\"\n","  ],\n","  \"entity_columns_absent\": []\n","}\n","\n","Input file inventory (SHA-256 of raw bytes):\n","                 file     bytes                                                           sha256\n","   train_identity.csv  26529680 b63c725d8377be90a995268d97f347c17d456b95db45807adcf9f59cd603c37c\n","train_transaction.csv 683351067 3a5c83ab6b3cc13dcabe5ffa9f522307fd5f7f7b6e6f6a60c32284ca6283d642\n"]}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 2 - data loading and schema validation.\"\"\"\n","\n","CANDIDATE_DIRS = [\n","    \"/kaggle/input/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","    \"/kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","    \"./data/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","    \"./data\",\n","]\n","\n","REQUIRED_TRANSACTION_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"TransactionID\", \"isFraud\", \"TransactionDT\", \"TransactionAmt\", \"ProductCD\",\n","    \"card1\", \"addr1\", \"P_emaildomain\",\n","]\n","OPTIONAL_ENTITY_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"card1\", \"card2\", \"card3\", \"card4\", \"card5\", \"card6\",\n","    \"addr1\", \"addr2\", \"P_emaildomain\", \"R_emaildomain\",\n","    \"DeviceInfo\", \"DeviceType\",\n","]\n","# Columns that describe the label or the split itself and must never be predictors.\n","TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"isFraud\", \"TransactionID\", \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"elapsed_days\", \"day_index\", \"chrono_block\",\n","]\n","\n","\n","def resolve_data_dir(candidates: Sequence[str]) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Return the first existing directory that contains train_transaction.csv.\n","\n","    Raises:\n","        FileNotFoundError: with every path tried, so the fix is obvious.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    for directory in candidates:\n","        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(directory, \"train_transaction.csv\")):\n","            return directory\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(\n","        \"train_transaction.csv was not found. Directories tried: \"\n","        f\"{list(candidates)}. Attach the IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection dataset or set \"\n","        \"CANDIDATE_DIRS to the local path.\"\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def validate_schema(\n","    frame: pd.DataFrame,\n","    required: Sequence[str],\n","    optional: Sequence[str] = (),\n","    name: str = \"dataframe\",\n",") -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"Assert required columns exist; record which optional columns are absent.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        frame: dataframe to validate.\n","        required: columns whose absence is fatal.\n","        optional: columns whose absence is recorded, not fatal.\n","        name: label used in error messages.\n","\n","    Returns:\n","        dict with present_required, present_optional, missing_optional, n_rows.\n","\n","    Raises:\n","        KeyError: naming every missing required column at once.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if not isinstance(frame, pd.DataFrame):\n","        raise TypeError(\"validate_schema expects a pandas DataFrame.\")\n","    cols = set(frame.columns)\n","    missing_required = [c for c in required if c not in cols]\n","    if missing_required:\n","        raise KeyError(\n","            f\"{name} is missing required column(s): {missing_required}. \"\n","            \"The notebook cannot proceed without them.\"\n","        )\n","    missing_optional = [c for c in optional if c not in cols]\n","    report = {\n","        \"present_required\": list(required),\n","        \"present_optional\": [c for c in optional if c in cols],\n","        \"missing_optional\": missing_optional,\n","        \"n_rows\": int(len(frame)),\n","    }\n","    if missing_optional:\n","        LOG.warning(\"%s: optional columns absent, analyses that need them are skipped: %s\",\n","                    name, missing_optional)\n","    return report\n","\n","\n","def reduce_memory(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Downcast numeric columns in place-ish to keep the merged frame in RAM.\n","\n","    Integers shrink to the smallest safe integer type; floats become float32,\n","    which preserves NaN and is ample for the diagnostics computed here. Object\n","    columns are left untouched.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    before = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    for col in frame.columns:\n","        kind = frame[col].dtype.kind\n","        if kind == \"i\":\n","            frame[col] = pd.to_numeric(frame[col], downcast=\"integer\")\n","        elif kind == \"f\":\n","            frame[col] = frame[col].astype(np.float32)\n","    after = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    LOG.info(\"Memory %.0f MB -> %.0f MB (%.0f%% saved)\",\n","             before, after, 100 * (before - after) / max(before, 1e-9))\n","    return frame\n","\n","\n","DATA_DIR = resolve_data_dir(CANDIDATE_DIRS)\n","LOG.info(\"Reading IEEE-CIS data from %s\", DATA_DIR)\n","\n","INPUT_INVENTORY = [\n","    hash_file(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, f))\n","    for f in sorted(os.listdir(DATA_DIR))\n","    if f.endswith(\".csv\") and f.startswith(\"train_\")\n","]\n","\n","transactions = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"train_transaction.csv\"))\n","# Device columns live in the identity table, so they are checked after the merge.\n","validate_schema(transactions, REQUIRED_TRANSACTION_COLUMNS,\n","                [c for c in OPTIONAL_ENTITY_COLUMNS\n","                 if c not in (\"DeviceInfo\", \"DeviceType\")],\n","                name=\"train_transaction\")\n","\n","identity_path = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"train_identity.csv\")\n","if os.path.exists(identity_path):\n","    identity = pd.read_csv(identity_path)\n","    validate_schema(identity, [ID_COLUMN], [\"DeviceType\", \"DeviceInfo\"],\n","                    name=\"train_identity\")\n","    df = transactions.merge(identity, on=ID_COLUMN, how=\"left\")\n","    identity_available = True\n","    del identity\n","else:\n","    LOG.warning(\"train_identity.csv absent - identity/device analyses are recorded \"\n","                \"as not computed rather than skipped silently.\")\n","    df = transactions.copy()\n","    identity_available = False\n","del transactions\n","gc.collect()\n","\n","# The left join must not create or drop rows, and the label must be clean.\n","assert df[ID_COLUMN].is_unique, \"Duplicate TransactionID after the identity merge.\"\n","assert df[TIME_COLUMN].notna().all(), \"TransactionDT contains missing values.\"\n","assert df[TARGET_COLUMN].notna().all(), \"isFraud contains missing values.\"\n","assert set(pd.unique(df[TARGET_COLUMN])) <= {0, 1}, \"isFraud is not strictly 0/1.\"\n","\n","df = reduce_memory(df)\n","\n","IDENTITY_COLUMNS = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"id_\")] + \\\n","                   [c for c in (\"DeviceType\", \"DeviceInfo\") if c in df.columns]\n","D_SERIES = sorted([c for c in df.columns\n","                   if len(c) > 1 and c[0] == \"D\" and c[1:].isdigit()],\n","                  key=lambda c: int(c[1:]))\n","V_SERIES = sorted([c for c in df.columns\n","                   if len(c) > 1 and c[0] == \"V\" and c[1:].isdigit()],\n","                  key=lambda c: int(c[1:]))\n","ENTITY_COLUMNS = [c for c in OPTIONAL_ENTITY_COLUMNS if c in df.columns]\n","ENTITY_COLUMNS_MISSING = [c for c in OPTIONAL_ENTITY_COLUMNS if c not in df.columns]\n","\n","SCHEMA_REPORT = {\n","    \"rows\": int(len(df)),\n","    \"columns\": int(df.shape[1]),\n","    \"identity_table_available\": identity_available,\n","    \"n_identity_columns\": len(IDENTITY_COLUMNS),\n","    \"n_d_series\": len(D_SERIES),\n","    \"n_v_series\": len(V_SERIES),\n","    \"entity_columns_available\": ENTITY_COLUMNS,\n","    \"entity_columns_absent\": ENTITY_COLUMNS_MISSING,\n","    \"input_files\": INPUT_INVENTORY,\n","}\n","if ENTITY_COLUMNS_MISSING:\n","    LOG.warning(\"Candidate entity columns absent from the merged frame; their \"\n","                \"Section 8 analyses are recorded as not computed: %s\",\n","                ENTITY_COLUMNS_MISSING)\n","if not D_SERIES:\n","    raise KeyError(\"No D-series columns found; Section 5 cannot run on this schema.\")\n","if not V_SERIES:\n","    LOG.warning(\"No V-series columns found; Section 7 will be recorded as not computed.\")\n","\n","print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in SCHEMA_REPORT.items() if k != \"input_files\"}, indent=2))\n","print(\"\\nInput file inventory (SHA-256 of raw bytes):\")\n","print(pd.DataFrame(INPUT_INVENTORY).to_string(index=False))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d57182e2","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"838bae1d-a340-4499-93fc-aa9cf9bf3d40","_uuid":"e2f181d3-e46f-4adf-8799-d07d74959539","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.009889,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.739221+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.729332+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Interpreting Section 2\n","\n","The four assertions after the merge check the things a join can break: key\n","uniqueness, a complete time column, a complete target and a strictly binary\n","target. Any failure stops the notebook here rather than propagating a corrupted\n","frame into the split."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e32c9556","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"8868ccfe-a15e-45f8-9d44-e980618ab82a","_uuid":"a4ebb49a-fa69-4af1-b865-1443d800c464","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.009966,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.759091+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.749125+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3. Temporal Split and OOT Quarantine — the protocol invariant\n","\n","Blocks 1..4 are development. Block 5 is the out-of-time holdout.\n","\n","**The invariant, stated as it is enforced.** No preprocessing object, statistic,\n","imputation value, category map, frequency encoding, scaling parameter, bin edge,\n","feature-selection score, mutual-information score, cluster representative or\n","decision threshold in this notebook is estimated from block 5. OOT is transformed\n","using development-learned parameters and evaluated only after every development\n","decision is final; OOT diagnostics are reported as evidence and never feed back\n","into a fitted object or a selected feature.\n","\n","This is enforced three ways, not asserted once:\n","\n","1. **Executable assertions** — `assert_oot_quarantine` checks temporal ordering,\n","   identifier disjointness, block exclusivity and ordering, and the exclusion of\n","   target-leakage columns from the predictor set.\n","2. **A guard at the call site** — any frame about to be passed to a fit,\n","   selection, threshold search or clustering call goes through `AUDITOR.guard`,\n","   which raises if it contains a quarantined identifier.\n","3. **A provenance registry** — every fitted object registers the rows and blocks\n","   it was fitted on. The registry is exported in `run_manifest.json`, so the\n","   claim is auditable after the fact rather than taken on trust."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"5cc23d33","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"53ced78d-185d-4dd2-a6e3-4e243184369a","_uuid":"a2e69366-2f5b-46a4-9f78-4e129ed22e64","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.781282Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.780708Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.184705Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.183693Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":5.41776,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.18678+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:23.76902+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:12:28 | INFO    | CHECK oot_strictly_after_dev                     PASS dev max 12192842 < oot min 12192900\n","09:12:28 | INFO    | CHECK row_identifiers_disjoint                   PASS 472,432 dev ids, 118,108 oot ids, 0 shared\n","09:12:28 | INFO    | CHECK blocks_mutually_exclusive                  PASS dev [1, 2, 3, 4] / oot [5]\n","09:12:28 | INFO    | CHECK blocks_ordered_in_time                     PASS each block ends no later than the next block starts\n","09:12:28 | INFO    | CHECK target_leakage_columns_excluded            PASS none present\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":[" chrono_block   rows  start_day    end_day  frauds  missing_target  span_days  fraud_rate_pct role\n","            1 118108   0.000000  25.737709  2826.0             0.0  25.740000           2.393  dev\n","            2 118108  25.738020  63.725731  4732.0             0.0  37.990002           4.007  dev\n","            3 118108  63.725742 100.224213  4430.0             0.0  36.500000           3.751  dev\n","            4 118108 100.224510 140.120850  4611.0             0.0  39.900002           3.904  dev\n","            5 118108 140.121521 181.999207     NaN             NaN  41.880001             NaN  OOT\n","\n","Leakage checks:\n","                          check  passed                                              detail\n","         oot_strictly_after_dev    True                 dev max 12192842 < oot min 12192900\n","       row_identifiers_disjoint    True          472,432 dev ids, 118,108 oot ids, 0 shared\n","      blocks_mutually_exclusive    True                          dev [1, 2, 3, 4] / oot [5]\n","         blocks_ordered_in_time    True each block ends no later than the next block starts\n","target_leakage_columns_excluded    True                                        none present\n","\n","Data hash: 562be68158df3e8a3ab5f7ec5bd7d4d5b5e75a10676f930671d1f17a7fe69f31\n","Total observed span: 182.0 elapsed days. TransactionDT is a relative offset, so block spans are elapsed-time statements only - no calendar month is claimed.\n"]}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 3 - temporal split, OOT quarantine and the leakage auditor.\"\"\"\n","\n","\n","def create_temporal_blocks(\n","    frame: pd.DataFrame,\n","    n_blocks: int,\n","    time_column: str = TIME_COLUMN,\n","    id_column: str = ID_COLUMN,\n",") -> pd.Series:\n","    \"\"\"Assign equal-row-count chronological block labels 1..n_blocks.\n","\n","    Rows are ordered by (time, id) with a stable sort, so the assignment is\n","    deterministic for a given frame regardless of its incoming order. Equal row\n","    counts (rather than equal durations) keep the per-block statistics\n","    comparable when traffic volume changes.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        frame: dataframe already containing ``time_column`` and ``id_column``.\n","        n_blocks: number of chronological blocks (>= 2).\n","        time_column: monotone time-ordering column.\n","        id_column: tie-breaker for identical timestamps.\n","\n","    Returns:\n","        Int16 Series of block labels aligned to ``frame.index``.\n","\n","    Raises:\n","        ValueError: for n_blocks < 2 or fewer rows than blocks.\n","        KeyError: if a column is absent.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if n_blocks < 2:\n","        raise ValueError(f\"n_blocks must be >= 2, got {n_blocks}.\")\n","    for col in (time_column, id_column):\n","        if col not in frame.columns:\n","            raise KeyError(f\"create_temporal_blocks requires column '{col}'.\")\n","    if len(frame) < n_blocks:\n","        raise ValueError(f\"{len(frame)} rows cannot be split into {n_blocks} blocks.\")\n","\n","    order = frame.sort_values([time_column, id_column], kind=\"mergesort\").index\n","    position = pd.Series(np.arange(len(order)), index=order)\n","    labels = np.minimum((position.values * n_blocks) // len(order), n_blocks - 1) + 1\n","    return pd.Series(labels.astype(np.int16), index=order).reindex(frame.index)\n","\n","\n","@dataclass\n","class FitProvenance:\n","    \"\"\"Record of what a fitted object was fitted on.\n","\n","    Every transformer, bin-edge set, selection score, cluster map or threshold\n","    produced in this notebook is registered here. The register is what makes\n","    \"no OOT was used\" an auditable claim instead of an assertion of good faith.\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    name: str\n","    kind: str\n","    fitted_on_blocks: Tuple[int, ...]\n","    n_rows_fitted: int\n","    row_id_hash: str\n","    created_at: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"))\n","\n","    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","        return {\n","            \"name\": self.name,\n","            \"kind\": self.kind,\n","            \"fitted_on_blocks\": list(self.fitted_on_blocks),\n","            \"n_rows_fitted\": self.n_rows_fitted,\n","            \"row_id_hash\": self.row_id_hash,\n","            \"created_at\": self.created_at,\n","        }\n","\n","\n","class LeakageAuditor:\n","    \"\"\"Reusable leakage-audit helper: registry + assertions + verdict log.\n","\n","    The auditor holds (a) the set of row identifiers quarantined as OOT, and\n","    (b) a registry of every fitted object with the blocks it was fitted on. Any\n","    registration whose fitting rows intersect the quarantine raises immediately.\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, oot_ids: Iterable[Any], oot_blocks: Iterable[int]) -> None:\n","        self._oot_ids = frozenset(np.asarray(list(oot_ids)).tolist())\n","        self._oot_blocks = frozenset(int(b) for b in oot_blocks)\n","        self.registry: List[FitProvenance] = []\n","        self.checks: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n","\n","    @staticmethod\n","    def _hash_ids(ids: Sequence[Any]) -> str:\n","        arr = np.sort(np.asarray(ids))\n","        return hashlib.sha256(np.ascontiguousarray(arr).tobytes()).hexdigest()[:16]\n","\n","    def register_fit(self, name: str, kind: str, fitted_ids: Sequence[Any],\n","                     fitted_blocks: Iterable[int]) -> FitProvenance:\n","        \"\"\"Register a fitted object and fail closed if it touched OOT rows.\"\"\"\n","        ids = np.asarray(fitted_ids)\n","        blocks = tuple(sorted(int(b) for b in fitted_blocks))\n","        overlap_blocks = self._oot_blocks.intersection(blocks)\n","        if overlap_blocks:\n","            raise AssertionError(\n","                f\"LEAKAGE: '{name}' declares a fit on OOT block(s) {sorted(overlap_blocks)}.\"\n","            )\n","        overlap_ids = self._oot_ids.intersection(ids.tolist())\n","        if overlap_ids:\n","            raise AssertionError(\n","                f\"LEAKAGE: '{name}' was fitted on {len(overlap_ids)} quarantined OOT row(s).\"\n","            )\n","        record = FitProvenance(name=name, kind=kind, fitted_on_blocks=blocks,\n","                               n_rows_fitted=int(ids.size),\n","                               row_id_hash=self._hash_ids(ids))\n","        self.registry.append(record)\n","        return record\n","\n","    def guard(self, name: str, frame: pd.DataFrame, id_column: str = ID_COLUMN) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","        \"\"\"Return ``frame`` unchanged after proving it holds no quarantined row.\n","\n","        Wrap any frame that is about to be passed to fit/fit_transform, a\n","        feature-selection score, a threshold search or a clustering call.\n","        \"\"\"\n","        overlap = self._oot_ids.intersection(frame[id_column].tolist())\n","        if overlap:\n","            raise AssertionError(\n","                f\"LEAKAGE: '{name}' received {len(overlap)} OOT row(s). \"\n","                \"Fitting, selection, thresholding and clustering are development-only.\"\n","            )\n","        return frame\n","\n","    def record_check(self, name: str, passed: bool, detail: str = \"\") -> bool:\n","        self.checks.append({\"check\": name, \"passed\": bool(passed), \"detail\": detail})\n","        (LOG.info if passed else LOG.error)(\"CHECK %-42s %s %s\",\n","                                            name, \"PASS\" if passed else \"FAIL\", detail)\n","        return passed\n","\n","    def summary(self) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","        return pd.DataFrame(self.checks)\n","\n","\n","def require(condition: bool, message: str) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Raise explicitly when a protocol invariant is violated.\n","\n","    This intentionally does not use Python's ``assert`` statement because asserts\n","    can be disabled with optimized interpreter settings.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if not condition:\n","        raise AssertionError(message)\n","\n","\n","def assert_oot_quarantine(dev: pd.DataFrame, oot: pd.DataFrame,\n","                          auditor: \"LeakageAuditor\",\n","                          time_column: str = TIME_COLUMN,\n","                          id_column: str = ID_COLUMN,\n","                          predictors: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Run and log the invariant checks that define the temporal protocol.\n","\n","    Returns the auditor's check table. Raises AssertionError on the strict\n","    invariants (temporal ordering and identifier disjointness); softer checks\n","    are logged with a pass/fail flag.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    require(oot[time_column].min() > dev[time_column].max(),\n","            \"OOT overlaps the development period\")\n","    auditor.record_check(\"oot_strictly_after_dev\", True,\n","                         f\"dev max {dev[time_column].max()} < oot min {oot[time_column].min()}\")\n","\n","    dev_ids, oot_ids = set(dev[id_column]), set(oot[id_column])\n","    require(not dev_ids & oot_ids, \"Development and OOT row identifiers overlap\")\n","    auditor.record_check(\"row_identifiers_disjoint\", True,\n","                         f\"{len(dev_ids):,} dev ids, {len(oot_ids):,} oot ids, 0 shared\")\n","\n","    blocks = pd.concat([dev[\"chrono_block\"], oot[\"chrono_block\"]])\n","    dev_blocks, oot_blocks = set(dev[\"chrono_block\"]), set(oot[\"chrono_block\"])\n","    auditor.record_check(\"blocks_mutually_exclusive\", not (dev_blocks & oot_blocks),\n","                         f\"dev {sorted(dev_blocks)} / oot {sorted(oot_blocks)}\")\n","    require(not (dev_blocks & oot_blocks),\n","            f\"Development and OOT blocks overlap: {sorted(dev_blocks & oot_blocks)}\")\n","\n","    bounds = (pd.concat([dev, oot])\n","              .groupby(\"chrono_block\")[time_column].agg([\"min\", \"max\"])\n","              .sort_index())\n","    ordered = bool((bounds[\"max\"].values[:-1] <= bounds[\"min\"].values[1:]).all())\n","    auditor.record_check(\"blocks_ordered_in_time\", ordered,\n","                         \"each block ends no later than the next block starts\")\n","    require(ordered, \"Chronological blocks are not ordered in time.\")\n","\n","    if predictors is not None:\n","        offenders = [c for c in TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS if c in predictors]\n","        auditor.record_check(\"target_leakage_columns_excluded\", not offenders,\n","                             f\"offenders={offenders}\" if offenders else \"none present\")\n","        require(not offenders, f\"Predictor set contains leakage columns: {offenders}\")\n","    return auditor.summary()\n","\n","\n","# --- derive the split ------------------------------------------------------\n","df = df.sort_values([TIME_COLUMN, ID_COLUMN], kind=\"mergesort\").reset_index(drop=True)\n","T0 = int(df[TIME_COLUMN].min())\n","df[\"elapsed_days\"] = ((df[TIME_COLUMN] - T0) / CONFIG[\"SECONDS_PER_DAY\"]).astype(np.float32)\n","df[\"day_index\"] = ((df[TIME_COLUMN] - T0) // CONFIG[\"SECONDS_PER_DAY\"]).astype(np.int16)\n","df[\"chrono_block\"] = create_temporal_blocks(df, N_BLOCKS)\n","\n","DEV_MASK = df[\"chrono_block\"] < OOT_BLOCK\n","dev_df = df.loc[DEV_MASK]\n","oot_df = df.loc[~DEV_MASK]\n","\n","FEATURE_COLUMNS = [c for c in df.columns if c not in set(TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS)]\n","\n","AUDITOR = LeakageAuditor(oot_ids=oot_df[ID_COLUMN].to_numpy(), oot_blocks=[OOT_BLOCK])\n","CHECKS = assert_oot_quarantine(dev_df, oot_df, AUDITOR, predictors=FEATURE_COLUMNS)\n","\n","# Full-period profile uses only identifiers and time.\n","block_profile = (\n","    df.groupby(\"chrono_block\")\n","      .agg(rows=(ID_COLUMN, \"size\"),\n","           start_day=(\"elapsed_days\", \"min\"),\n","           end_day=(\"elapsed_days\", \"max\"))\n",")\n","\n","# Label summaries are calculated on development rows only.\n","dev_label_profile = (\n","    dev_df.groupby(\"chrono_block\")[TARGET_COLUMN]\n","          .agg(frauds=\"sum\",\n","               missing_target=lambda s: int(s.isna().sum()))\n",")\n","\n","block_profile = block_profile.join(dev_label_profile).reset_index()\n","block_profile[\"span_days\"] = (\n","    block_profile[\"end_day\"] - block_profile[\"start_day\"]\n",").round(2)\n","block_profile[\"fraud_rate_pct\"] = (\n","    100 * block_profile[\"frauds\"] / block_profile[\"rows\"]\n",").round(3)\n","block_profile[\"role\"] = np.where(\n","    block_profile[\"chrono_block\"] < OOT_BLOCK, \"dev\", \"OOT\"\n",")\n","\n","# Do not fingerprint sealed labels into the Stage 0 manifest.\n","DATA_HASH = compute_dataframe_hash(\n","    df,\n","    columns=[ID_COLUMN, TIME_COLUMN, \"chrono_block\"],\n","    sort_by=[TIME_COLUMN, ID_COLUMN],\n",")\n","DATA_HASH[\"development_target_sha256\"] = compute_dataframe_hash(\n","    dev_df,\n","    columns=[ID_COLUMN, TARGET_COLUMN],\n","    sort_by=[ID_COLUMN],\n",")[\"sha256\"]\n","\n","print(block_profile.to_string(index=False))\n","print(\"\\nLeakage checks:\")\n","print(CHECKS.to_string(index=False))\n","print(f\"\\nData hash: {DATA_HASH['sha256']}\")\n","print(f\"Total observed span: {df['elapsed_days'].max():.1f} elapsed days. \"\n","      \"TransactionDT is a relative offset, so block spans are elapsed-time \"\n","      \"statements only - no calendar month is claimed.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"55af42b4","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"0af38272-6300-4b5e-9287-c02d3f020ad0","_uuid":"3720445d-dc70-4dbd-a7de-888590247dd1","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.011778,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.209448+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.19767+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Interpreting Section 3\n","\n","`TransactionDT` is a **relative offset in seconds**, not a calendar timestamp.\n","Ordering and elapsed durations are therefore trustworthy; weekday, month and\n","holiday effects are not identifiable and are never claimed. The block table\n","reports each block's elapsed span in days precisely so that \"roughly a month\" can\n","be checked against the data instead of assumed: blocks are cut to **equal row\n","counts**, so their durations differ whenever traffic volume changes, and any\n","resemblance to a calendar month is a property of this dataset's traffic profile,\n","not a design guarantee."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b4ae55c1","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"60eff853-f8dd-4e1b-b6ba-10731c0e067e","_uuid":"bca4ae0e-42f4-4536-9736-77024d326720","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.010273,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.230733+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.22046+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4. Target–Time Analysis\n","\n","Per-block counts, positives, prevalence and Wilson intervals. Wilson rather than\n","the normal approximation: at ~3.5% prevalence the normal interval is unreliable\n","and can extend below zero."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"161d8d4a","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"9993db2e-aa77-4091-b901-e30401e19dd1","_uuid":"c589a163-3bb6-4b9b-ab8e-79e41cc2d999","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.253662Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.253048Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.857118Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.856299Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.618069,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.859237+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.241168+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":[" block role      n  missing_target  positives  prevalence_pct  ci_low_pct  ci_high_pct\n","     1  dev 118108               0       2826          2.3927      2.3071       2.4814\n","     2  dev 118108               0       4732          4.0065      3.8961       4.1199\n","     3  dev 118108               0       4430          3.7508      3.6439       3.8607\n","     4  dev 118108               0       4611          3.9041      3.7951       4.0160\n","\n","Dev-block prevalence homogeneity: chi2=595.1, p=1.18e-128, Cramer's V=0.0355 (effect size, not the p-value, is the quantity to judge at n>400k).\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1210x605 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 770x352 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 4 - target prevalence over time and the deferred evaluation function.\"\"\"\n","\n","\n","def wilson_interval(successes: int, n: int, z: float = 1.96) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n","    \"\"\"Wilson score interval for a proportion; reliable at low prevalence.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        successes: count of positives (>= 0).\n","        n: total trials (>= 0). Returns (nan, nan) when n == 0.\n","        z: normal quantile; 1.96 is the two-sided 95% interval.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if n < 0 or successes < 0 or successes > max(n, 0):\n","        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid counts: successes={successes}, n={n}.\")\n","    if n == 0:\n","        return (float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\"))\n","    p = successes / n\n","    denom = 1 + z ** 2 / n\n","    centre = (p + z ** 2 / (2 * n)) / denom\n","    half = z * np.sqrt(p * (1 - p) / n + z ** 2 / (4 * n ** 2)) / denom\n","    return (max(0.0, centre - half), min(1.0, centre + half))\n","\n","\n","def prevalence_by_block(frame: pd.DataFrame, target: str = TARGET_COLUMN,\n","                        block_column: str = \"chrono_block\",\n","                        oot_block: int = OOT_BLOCK) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Per-block row count, positives, prevalence and a Wilson 95% interval.\"\"\"\n","    if target not in frame.columns or block_column not in frame.columns:\n","        raise KeyError(f\"prevalence_by_block requires '{target}' and '{block_column}'.\")\n","    rows = []\n","    for block, sub in frame.groupby(block_column, sort=True)[target]:\n","        n, k = int(len(sub)), int(sub.sum())\n","        lo, hi = wilson_interval(k, n)\n","        rows.append({\n","            \"block\": int(block),\n","            \"role\": \"OOT\" if int(block) >= oot_block else \"dev\",\n","            \"n\": n,\n","            \"missing_target\": int(sub.isna().sum()),\n","            \"positives\": k,\n","            \"prevalence_pct\": round(100 * k / n, 4) if n else float(\"nan\"),\n","            \"ci_low_pct\": round(100 * lo, 4),\n","            \"ci_high_pct\": round(100 * hi, 4),\n","        })\n","    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","\n","\n","def recall_at_fixed_fpr(y_true: Sequence[int], y_score: Sequence[float],\n","                        fpr: float = CONFIG[\"FIXED_FPR\"]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"Recall at a fixed false-positive rate, with its denominators stated.\n","\n","    The score threshold is the (1 - fpr) quantile of the NEGATIVE-class scores,\n","    so the realised FPR is as close to the target as the negative sample allows.\n","\n","    This notebook produces no model, so this function is defined for the\n","    modelling stage and is NOT invoked on real data here. Calling it on absent\n","    predictions would fabricate a result; it therefore stays unused until a\n","    model exists. It is exercised only in the synthetic checks (Section 14).\n","    \"\"\"\n","    y_true = np.asarray(y_true)\n","    y_score = np.asarray(y_score, dtype=float)\n","    if y_true.shape != y_score.shape:\n","        raise ValueError(\"y_true and y_score must have the same shape.\")\n","    if not 0 < fpr < 1:\n","        raise ValueError(f\"fpr must lie in (0, 1), got {fpr}.\")\n","    neg, pos = y_score[y_true == 0], y_score[y_true == 1]\n","    if neg.size == 0 or pos.size == 0:\n","        raise ValueError(\"Both classes must be present to evaluate recall at a fixed FPR.\")\n","    threshold = float(np.quantile(neg, 1 - fpr))\n","    flagged_neg = int((neg >= threshold).sum())\n","    flagged_pos = int((pos >= threshold).sum())\n","    return {\n","        \"threshold\": threshold,\n","        \"target_fpr\": fpr,\n","        \"realised_fpr\": flagged_neg / neg.size,\n","        \"recall\": flagged_pos / pos.size,\n","        \"n_negatives\": int(neg.size),\n","        \"n_positives\": int(pos.size),\n","        \"denominator_note\": (\"recall denominator = positives in the evaluated block; \"\n","                             \"FPR denominator = negatives in the evaluated block\"),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","PREVALENCE = prevalence_by_block(dev_df)\n","print(PREVALENCE.to_string(index=False))\n","\n","_dev_prev = PREVALENCE[PREVALENCE.role == \"dev\"]\n","_table = np.array([_dev_prev[\"positives\"].to_numpy(),\n","                   (_dev_prev[\"n\"] - _dev_prev[\"positives\"]).to_numpy()])\n","_chi2, _p, _, _ = stats.chi2_contingency(_table)\n","_cramers_v = float(np.sqrt(_chi2 / (_table.sum() * (min(_table.shape) - 1))))\n","PRIOR_SHIFT = {\"chi2\": float(_chi2), \"p_value\": float(_p), \"cramers_v\": _cramers_v,\n","               \"blocks_compared\": _dev_prev[\"block\"].tolist()}\n","print(f\"\\nDev-block prevalence homogeneity: chi2={_chi2:,.1f}, p={_p:.3g}, \"\n","      f\"Cramer's V={_cramers_v:.4f} (effect size, not the p-value, is the \"\n","      \"quantity to judge at n>400k).\")\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(11, 5.5), sharex=True)\n","\n","_daily_volume = (\n","df.groupby(\"day_index\")\n",".agg(n=(ID_COLUMN, \"size\"))\n",".reset_index()\n",")\n","\n","_daily_dev_rate = (\n","dev_df.groupby(\"day_index\")[TARGET_COLUMN]\n",".mean()\n",".reset_index(name=\"rate\")\n",")\n","\n","axes[0].plot(_daily_volume.day_index, _daily_volume.n, lw=0.9)\n","axes[0].set_ylabel(\"transactions per day\")\n","axes[0].set_title(\"Volume and fraud prevalence over elapsed time \"\n","                  f\"(dotted line = start of OOT block {OOT_BLOCK})\")\n","axes[1].plot(\n","    _daily_dev_rate.day_index,\n","    100 * _daily_dev_rate.rate,\n","    lw=0.9,\n","    color=\"crimson\",\n","    label=\"development daily prevalence\",\n",")\n","axes[1].axhline(100 * df.loc[DEV_MASK, TARGET_COLUMN].mean(), ls=\"--\", c=\"grey\",\n","                lw=1, label=\"development mean\")\n","axes[1].set_ylabel(\"fraud prevalence (%)\")\n","axes[1].set_xlabel(\"elapsed day (relative to first transaction)\")\n","_oot_start_day = int(df.loc[~DEV_MASK, \"day_index\"].min())\n","for ax in axes:\n","    ax.axvline(_oot_start_day, color=\"black\", ls=\":\", lw=1.2)\n","axes[1].legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=8)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 3.2))\n","ax.errorbar(PREVALENCE.block, PREVALENCE.prevalence_pct,\n","            yerr=[PREVALENCE.prevalence_pct - PREVALENCE.ci_low_pct,\n","                  PREVALENCE.ci_high_pct - PREVALENCE.prevalence_pct],\n","            fmt=\"o\", capsize=4)\n","ax.set_xticks(PREVALENCE.block)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"chronological block\")\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"fraud prevalence (%)\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Fraud prevalence by block with Wilson 95% intervals\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"818781d7","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"39891086-9354-49d4-8069-43ba46fbfef0","_uuid":"35df87cd-91e1-4027-abfa-2835d190a128","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.012712,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.885714+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.873002+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Interpreting Section 4 — prior shift and why thresholds are period-specific\n","\n","If prevalence differs across blocks, a score threshold calibrated on one period\n","delivers a different alert volume and a different precision in the next, even\n","with an unchanged model. Two consequences follow, and both are protocol rather\n","than preference:\n","\n","* an operating threshold must be **assessed per period**, not fixed once on the\n","  pooled development data;\n","* per-block **lift is computed against that block's own prevalence** (Section 5),\n","  so a prior shift cannot masquerade as feature signal.\n","\n","Note the sample-size effect in the homogeneity test: at n > 400,000 an\n","inconsequential difference in prevalence produces an astronomically small\n","p-value. Cramér's V is the quantity to read.\n","\n","**No model exists in this notebook, so no recall at 0.1% FPR is reported.**\n","`recall_at_fixed_fpr` is defined, documented and exercised on synthetic data in\n","Section 14, ready for the modelling stage. Reporting a number here would be\n","fabrication."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9b5080b9","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"d881e067-e270-4d87-9427-884e0ac3aa8c","_uuid":"60db1f34-32ac-4d98-b894-d13380820922","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.013359,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.912109+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.89875+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5. D-Series Temporal Risk Analysis\n","\n","Five reusable diagnostics, applied to the numeric battery (amount, D-series,\n","C-series, distances, V-series):\n","\n","* **PSI** with bin edges learned on the development reference block and reused\n","  unchanged for every comparison including OOT; a documented epsilon floor for\n","  empty bins; a separate MISSING bin; sample counts reported alongside.\n","* **Two-sample KS**, block 1 versus block 4 (both development), with statistic,\n","  p-value, both non-missing sample sizes and a Benjamini–Hochberg adjusted\n","  p-value.\n","* **Spearman** correlation with elapsed time.\n","* **Per-block top-decile fraud lift**, with the cut point learned on development\n","  data and lift taken against each block's own prevalence.\n","* **Lift stability**, defined explicitly as `1 − std(lift)/mean(lift)` over\n","  development blocks, withheld entirely when too few blocks carry enough\n","  positives.\n","\n","The PSI bands (`< 0.10` stable, `0.10–0.25` moderate, `> 0.25` severe) are\n","**configured decision rules**, not universal laws, and PSI is a divergence, not\n","a hypothesis test — it has no p-value here and none is implied."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"7885dd26","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"80b33a5d-2379-4e87-b5b6-969ae21cf5e7","_uuid":"f2c91664-6254-42c1-b41f-b33a788c730b","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.940349Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.940046Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.978762Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.977856Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.055367,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.980574+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.925207+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:12:29 | INFO    | Drift, association and lift functions defined.\n"]}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 5a - reusable drift, association and lift functions.\"\"\"\n","\n","\n","def learn_psi_bins(reference: Sequence[float], bins: int = CONFIG[\"PSI_BINS\"]) -> Optional[np.ndarray]:\n","    \"\"\"Learn PSI bin edges from REFERENCE (development) values only.\n","\n","    Quantile edges are de-duplicated, so a low-variance feature simply yields\n","    fewer bins rather than an error. Returns None when fewer than two distinct\n","    edges survive (a constant feature), which callers treat as \"not assessable\".\n","    \"\"\"\n","    values = pd.Series(reference).dropna().to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","    values = values[np.isfinite(values)]\n","    if values.size == 0:\n","        return None\n","    edges = np.unique(np.quantile(values, np.linspace(0, 1, bins + 1)))\n","    if edges.size < 2:\n","        return None\n","    edges[0], edges[-1] = -np.inf, np.inf\n","    return edges\n","\n","\n","def calculate_psi(reference: Sequence[float], comparison: Sequence[float],\n","                  edges: Optional[np.ndarray] = None,\n","                  bins: int = CONFIG[\"PSI_BINS\"],\n","                  epsilon: float = CONFIG[\"PSI_EPSILON\"],\n","                  include_missing_bin: bool = True) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"Population Stability Index of ``comparison`` against ``reference``.\n","\n","    PSI = sum over bins of (p_comp - p_ref) * ln(p_comp / p_ref).\n","\n","    Design decisions, all explicit:\n","      * Bin edges are learned from the reference sample only (or supplied by the\n","        caller, which is how development edges are reused for OOT).\n","      * Zero proportions are floored at ``epsilon`` (default 1e-6) before the\n","        logarithm, so an empty bin contributes a large-but-finite term instead\n","        of infinity. The floor is reported in the result.\n","      * When ``include_missing_bin``, missingness forms its own bin, so a\n","        feature that silently stops being populated registers as drift.\n","\n","    PSI is a descriptive divergence, not a hypothesis test: it has no p-value\n","    and no null distribution here.\n","\n","    Returns:\n","        dict with psi, n_reference, n_comparison, n_bins, bin_table,\n","        assessable and (when not assessable) reason.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    ref = pd.Series(reference)\n","    cmp_ = pd.Series(comparison)\n","    ref_missing, cmp_missing = int(ref.isna().sum()), int(cmp_.isna().sum())\n","    ref_v = ref.dropna().to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","    cmp_v = cmp_.dropna().to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","    ref_v, cmp_v = ref_v[np.isfinite(ref_v)], cmp_v[np.isfinite(cmp_v)]\n","\n","    if edges is None:\n","        edges = learn_psi_bins(ref_v, bins=bins)\n","    if edges is None or ref_v.size == 0 or cmp_v.size == 0:\n","        return {\"psi\": float(\"nan\"), \"assessable\": False,\n","                \"reason\": \"constant, empty or all-missing reference/comparison\",\n","                \"n_reference\": int(ref_v.size), \"n_comparison\": int(cmp_v.size),\n","                \"n_bins\": 0, \"epsilon\": epsilon, \"bin_table\": None}\n","\n","    ref_counts = np.histogram(ref_v, bins=edges)[0].astype(float)\n","    cmp_counts = np.histogram(cmp_v, bins=edges)[0].astype(float)\n","    labels = [f\"({edges[i]:.6g}, {edges[i + 1]:.6g}]\" for i in range(len(edges) - 1)]\n","    if include_missing_bin and (ref_missing or cmp_missing):\n","        ref_counts = np.append(ref_counts, ref_missing)\n","        cmp_counts = np.append(cmp_counts, cmp_missing)\n","        labels.append(\"MISSING\")\n","\n","    p_ref = np.clip(ref_counts / ref_counts.sum(), epsilon, None)\n","    p_cmp = np.clip(cmp_counts / cmp_counts.sum(), epsilon, None)\n","    contrib = (p_cmp - p_ref) * np.log(p_cmp / p_ref)\n","    return {\n","        \"psi\": float(contrib.sum()),\n","        \"assessable\": True,\n","        \"reason\": \"\",\n","        \"n_reference\": int(ref_counts.sum()),\n","        \"n_comparison\": int(cmp_counts.sum()),\n","        \"n_bins\": len(labels),\n","        \"epsilon\": epsilon,\n","        \"bin_table\": pd.DataFrame({\"bin\": labels, \"p_reference\": p_ref,\n","                                   \"p_comparison\": p_cmp, \"contribution\": contrib}),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def classify_psi(psi: float,\n","                 moderate: float = CONFIG[\"PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD\"],\n","                 severe: float = CONFIG[\"PSI_SEVERE_THRESHOLD\"]) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Map a PSI value onto the CONFIGURED bands (not universal constants).\"\"\"\n","    if psi is None or not np.isfinite(psi):\n","        return \"not_assessable\"\n","    if psi < moderate:\n","        return \"stable\"\n","    if psi <= severe:\n","        return \"moderate_drift\"\n","    return \"severe_drift\"\n","\n","\n","def calculate_feature_psi_by_block(frame: pd.DataFrame, feature: str,\n","                                   reference_block: int, comparison_blocks: Sequence[int],\n","                                   block_column: str = \"chrono_block\",\n","                                   bins: int = CONFIG[\"PSI_BINS\"]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"PSI of each comparison block against a fixed reference block.\n","\n","    Bin edges are learned once, on the reference block, and reused unchanged for\n","    every comparison block including OOT. That reuse is exactly what keeps the\n","    OOT transformation free of OOT-derived parameters.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if feature not in frame.columns:\n","        raise KeyError(f\"Unknown feature '{feature}'.\")\n","    ref_values = frame.loc[frame[block_column] == reference_block, feature]\n","    edges = learn_psi_bins(ref_values, bins=bins)\n","    rows = []\n","    for block in comparison_blocks:\n","        cmp_values = frame.loc[frame[block_column] == block, feature]\n","        result = calculate_psi(ref_values, cmp_values, edges=edges, bins=bins)\n","        rows.append({\"feature\": feature, \"reference_block\": reference_block,\n","                     \"comparison_block\": int(block), \"psi\": result[\"psi\"],\n","                     \"band\": classify_psi(result[\"psi\"]),\n","                     \"n_reference\": result[\"n_reference\"],\n","                     \"n_comparison\": result[\"n_comparison\"],\n","                     \"assessable\": result[\"assessable\"]})\n","    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","\n","\n","def run_ks_tests(frame: pd.DataFrame, features: Sequence[str],\n","                 block_a: int, block_b: int,\n","                 block_column: str = \"chrono_block\",\n","                 min_n: int = CONFIG[\"MIN_NON_MISSING\"]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Two-sample KS test of each feature between two blocks.\n","\n","    Reports the statistic (an effect size on the CDF scale), the raw p-value and\n","    both non-missing sample sizes. At IEEE-CIS sample sizes a p-value near zero\n","    is expected for trivially small differences, so the statistic - not the\n","    p-value - carries the practical meaning.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    a_frame = frame.loc[frame[block_column] == block_a]\n","    b_frame = frame.loc[frame[block_column] == block_b]\n","    rows = []\n","    for feature in features:\n","        a = a_frame[feature].dropna().to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","        b = b_frame[feature].dropna().to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","        a, b = a[np.isfinite(a)], b[np.isfinite(b)]\n","        if a.size < min_n or b.size < min_n:\n","            rows.append({\"feature\": feature, \"ks_stat\": np.nan, \"ks_pvalue\": np.nan,\n","                         \"n_a\": int(a.size), \"n_b\": int(b.size),\n","                         \"assessable\": False,\n","                         \"reason\": f\"fewer than {min_n} non-missing values in a block\"})\n","            continue\n","        result = stats.ks_2samp(a, b, method=\"asymp\")\n","        rows.append({\"feature\": feature, \"ks_stat\": float(result.statistic),\n","                     \"ks_pvalue\": float(result.pvalue),\n","                     \"n_a\": int(a.size), \"n_b\": int(b.size),\n","                     \"assessable\": True, \"reason\": \"\"})\n","    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","\n","\n","def adjust_multiple_tests(pvalues: Sequence[float], alpha: float = CONFIG[\"KS_ALPHA\"],\n","                          method: str = \"benjamini_hochberg\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-values and rejection flags.\n","\n","    NaN p-values (tests that could not be run) are carried through as NaN and\n","    excluded from the multiplicity count, so unrunnable tests neither inflate\n","    nor deflate the correction.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if method != \"benjamini_hochberg\":\n","        raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported correction '{method}'.\")\n","    p = np.asarray(pvalues, dtype=float)\n","    out_adj = np.full(p.shape, np.nan)\n","    out_rej = np.zeros(p.shape, dtype=bool)\n","    valid = np.where(np.isfinite(p))[0]\n","    if valid.size:\n","        pv = p[valid]\n","        order = np.argsort(pv, kind=\"mergesort\")\n","        ranked = pv[order]\n","        m = ranked.size\n","        adjusted = ranked * m / np.arange(1, m + 1)\n","        adjusted = np.minimum.accumulate(adjusted[::-1])[::-1]\n","        adjusted = np.clip(adjusted, 0, 1)\n","        restored = np.empty_like(adjusted)\n","        restored[order] = adjusted\n","        out_adj[valid] = restored\n","        out_rej[valid] = restored <= alpha\n","    return pd.DataFrame({\"pvalue\": p, \"adjusted_pvalue\": out_adj,\n","                         \"reject\": out_rej, \"alpha\": alpha, \"method\": method,\n","                         \"n_tests\": int(valid.size)})\n","\n","\n","def calculate_spearman_time_risk(frame: pd.DataFrame, features: Sequence[str],\n","                                 time_column: str = \"elapsed_days\",\n","                                 min_n: int = CONFIG[\"MIN_NON_MISSING\"]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Spearman rank correlation between each feature and elapsed time.\n","\n","    Spearman, not Pearson: temporal drift in these columns is monotone but not\n","    linear, and rank correlation is unaffected by the heavy right tails that\n","    dominate the V and D series.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    rows = []\n","    time_values = frame[time_column]\n","    for feature in features:\n","        series = frame[feature]\n","        mask = series.notna() & np.isfinite(series.astype(float)) & time_values.notna()\n","        n = int(mask.sum())\n","        if n < min_n or series[mask].nunique() < 2:\n","            rows.append({\"feature\": feature, \"spearman_corr_time\": np.nan,\n","                         \"spearman_pvalue\": np.nan, \"n\": n, \"assessable\": False,\n","                         \"reason\": \"insufficient non-missing values or constant\"})\n","            continue\n","        result = stats.spearmanr(series[mask].to_numpy(dtype=float),\n","                                 time_values[mask].to_numpy(dtype=float))\n","        rows.append({\"feature\": feature,\n","                     \"spearman_corr_time\": float(result.statistic),\n","                     \"spearman_pvalue\": float(result.pvalue),\n","                     \"n\": n, \"assessable\": True, \"reason\": \"\"})\n","    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","\n","\n","def calculate_top_decile_lift(frame: pd.DataFrame, feature: str,\n","                              cut_point: float, target: str = TARGET_COLUMN,\n","                              min_positives: int = CONFIG[\"MIN_POSITIVES_FOR_LIFT\"],\n","                              direction: str = \"upper\") -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"Fraud lift of the top decile of ``feature`` within one block.\n","\n","    The cut point is supplied by the caller (learned on development data) so\n","    that OOT never defines its own boundary. Lift is computed against the\n","    prevalence of the SAME block, so a block-level prior shift cannot be\n","    mistaken for feature signal.\n","\n","    Ties at the cut point are kept in the flagged group, and the realised\n","    flagged share is returned so a lumpy, low-variance feature is visible rather\n","    than silently mislabelled a \"decile\".\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if direction not in {\"upper\", \"lower\"}:\n","        raise ValueError(\"direction must be 'upper' or 'lower'.\")\n","    values, y = frame[feature], frame[target]\n","    mask = values.notna()\n","    n_valid = int(mask.sum())\n","    if n_valid == 0 or not np.isfinite(cut_point):\n","        return {\"feature\": feature, \"lift\": np.nan, \"assessable\": False,\n","                \"reason\": \"no non-missing values or undefined cut point\",\n","                \"n_evaluated\": n_valid, \"n_flagged\": 0, \"positives_flagged\": 0,\n","                \"flagged_share\": np.nan, \"block_prevalence\": np.nan}\n","    flagged = (values >= cut_point) if direction == \"upper\" else (values <= cut_point)\n","    flagged = flagged & mask\n","    n_flagged = int(flagged.sum())\n","    positives_flagged = int(y[flagged].sum())\n","    prevalence = float(y[mask].mean())\n","    if n_flagged == 0 or prevalence == 0:\n","        return {\"feature\": feature, \"lift\": np.nan, \"assessable\": False,\n","                \"reason\": \"empty flagged group or zero prevalence\",\n","                \"n_evaluated\": n_valid, \"n_flagged\": n_flagged,\n","                \"positives_flagged\": positives_flagged,\n","                \"flagged_share\": n_flagged / n_valid, \"block_prevalence\": prevalence}\n","    lift = (positives_flagged / n_flagged) / prevalence\n","    assessable = positives_flagged >= min_positives\n","    return {\"feature\": feature, \"lift\": float(lift), \"assessable\": assessable,\n","            \"reason\": \"\" if assessable else\n","                      f\"only {positives_flagged} positives in the flagged group \"\n","                      f\"(< {min_positives}); lift is unreliable\",\n","            \"n_evaluated\": n_valid, \"n_flagged\": n_flagged,\n","            \"positives_flagged\": positives_flagged,\n","            \"flagged_share\": n_flagged / n_valid, \"block_prevalence\": prevalence}\n","\n","\n","def calculate_lift_stability(lifts: Mapping[int, float],\n","                             min_blocks: int = CONFIG[\"LIFT_STABILITY_MIN_BLOCKS\"]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"Summarise how consistent a feature's top-decile lift is across blocks.\n","\n","    Definition used throughout this notebook:\n","\n","        lift_stability = 1 - (std(lift) / mean(lift))       [clipped to [0, 1]]\n","\n","    i.e. one minus the coefficient of variation of the per-block lift. 1.0 means\n","    identical lift in every block; 0.0 means the dispersion is as large as the\n","    mean. The metric is only returned when at least ``min_blocks`` blocks\n","    produced an assessable lift AND the mean lift is positive; otherwise the\n","    verdict is ``insufficient_evidence`` rather than a flattering number.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    usable = {int(b): float(v) for b, v in lifts.items()\n","              if v is not None and np.isfinite(v)}\n","    if len(usable) < min_blocks:\n","        return {\"lift_stability\": None, \"n_blocks\": len(usable),\n","                \"mean_lift\": None, \"std_lift\": None, \"direction\": None,\n","                \"verdict\": \"insufficient_evidence\",\n","                \"reason\": f\"assessable lift in only {len(usable)} block(s); \"\n","                          f\"{min_blocks} required\"}\n","    values = np.array([usable[b] for b in sorted(usable)])\n","    mean, std = float(values.mean()), float(values.std(ddof=1))\n","    if mean <= 0:\n","        return {\"lift_stability\": None, \"n_blocks\": len(usable), \"mean_lift\": mean,\n","                \"std_lift\": std, \"direction\": None, \"verdict\": \"insufficient_evidence\",\n","                \"reason\": \"non-positive mean lift; the ratio is undefined\"}\n","    stability = float(np.clip(1 - std / mean, 0.0, 1.0))\n","    direction = \"enriched\" if mean > 1 else (\"depleted\" if mean < 1 else \"neutral\")\n","    return {\"lift_stability\": stability, \"n_blocks\": len(usable), \"mean_lift\": mean,\n","            \"std_lift\": std, \"direction\": direction,\n","            \"verdict\": \"stable\" if stability >= CONFIG[\"LIFT_STABILITY_THRESHOLD\"] else \"unstable\", \"reason\": \"\"}\n","\n","\n","LOG.info(\"Drift, association and lift functions defined.\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"50924290","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"9f0acf53-9380-4d2b-ab20-245590ca60de","_uuid":"abf4b440-48e2-4436-bd6c-85f557429269","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:12:30.00889Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:12:30.008332Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.893167Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.891893Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":293.901914,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.895424+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:12:29.99351+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:12:30 | INFO    | Temporal-risk battery covers 371 numeric features.\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Workload estimate: 371 features x (3 dev PSI comparisons + 1 dev->OOT PSI + 4 development lift evaluations) on 590,540 rows; float32 columns are read one at a time.\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:17:23 | INFO    | Wrote ./artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv (371 features x 32 columns).\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  family               verdict  features\n","       C         moderate_risk         3\n","       C                stable         8\n","       C         temporal_risk         3\n","       D         moderate_risk         7\n","       D                stable         4\n","       D         temporal_risk         4\n","       V insufficient_evidence         1\n","       V         moderate_risk         2\n","       V                stable        80\n","       V         temporal_risk       256\n","  amount         moderate_risk         1\n","distance                stable         2\n","\n","D-series detail (the family the source notebook flagged as range-expanding):\n","feature  development_non_missing_count  PSI_max_development_only  ks_stat  ks_adjusted_pvalue  spearman_corr_time  lift_stability  missingness_drift       verdict       action\n","     D1                         471496                  0.178495 0.162745        0.000000e+00            0.091844        0.739975           0.000838 moderate_risk      monitor\n","    D10                         406041                  0.533464 0.085557       7.290226e-290            0.012588        0.780371          -0.058986 temporal_risk tag_not_drop\n","    D11                         226459                  0.696693 0.092141       3.164170e-170            0.086324             NaN          -0.238589 temporal_risk tag_not_drop\n","    D12                          52703                  0.003321 0.067878        1.989032e-26            0.062099        0.914060           0.009836        stable         keep\n","    D13                          48973                  0.003550 0.039237        2.484559e-08            0.035407        0