Section 5b - run the temporal-risk battery and build feature_risk_table.csv.\"\"\"\n","\n","\n","def family_of(column: str) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Assign a column to its IEEE-CIS feature family (working interpretation).\"\"\"\n","    if column == \"TransactionAmt\":\n","        return \"amount\"\n","    if column == \"ProductCD\":\n","        return \"product\"\n","    if column.startswith(\"card\"):\n","        return \"entity\"\n","    if column.startswith(\"addr\"):\n","        return \"entity\"\n","    if column.endswith(\"emaildomain\"):\n","        return \"entity\"\n","    if column in (\"DeviceType\", \"DeviceInfo\"):\n","        return \"entity\"\n","    if column.startswith(\"dist\"):\n","        return \"distance\"\n","    if len(column) > 1 and column[0] == \"C\" and column[1:].isdigit():\n","        return \"C\"\n","    if len(column) > 1 and column[0] == \"D\" and column[1:].isdigit():\n","        return \"D\"\n","    if len(column) > 1 and column[0] == \"M\" and column[1:].isdigit():\n","        return \"M\"\n","    if len(column) > 1 and column[0] == \"V\" and column[1:].isdigit():\n","        return \"V\"\n","    if column.startswith(\"id_\"):\n","        return \"identity\"\n","    return \"other\"\n","\n","\n","NUMERIC_FEATURES = [c for c in FEATURE_COLUMNS if df[c].dtype.kind in \"if\"]\n","C_SERIES = sorted([c for c in NUMERIC_FEATURES if family_of(c) == \"C\"],\n","                  key=lambda c: int(c[1:]))\n","# The audit battery: D-series (the temporal-risk family of interest), the\n","# amount, distances and counting features, plus every numeric V column. All\n","# statistics below are computed on development rows unless a cell says\n","# otherwise; OOT enters only as a *comparison* sample against dev-learned edges.\n","AUDIT_FEATURES = [c for c in ([\"TransactionAmt\"] + D_SERIES + C_SERIES + V_SERIES\n","                              + [c for c in (\"dist1\", \"dist2\") if c in df.columns])\n","                  if c in NUMERIC_FEATURES]\n","AUDIT_FEATURES = sorted(set(AUDIT_FEATURES), key=AUDIT_FEATURES.index)\n","LOG.info(\"Temporal-risk battery covers %d numeric features.\", len(AUDIT_FEATURES))\n","\n","# --- estimated workload, printed before the expensive loop -------------------\n","print(f\"Workload estimate: {len(AUDIT_FEATURES)} features x \"\n","      f\"({len(DEV_BLOCKS) - 1} dev PSI comparisons + 1 dev->OOT PSI + \"\n","      f\"{len(DEV_BLOCKS)} development lift evaluations) \"\n","      f\"on {len(df):,} rows; float32 columns are read one at a time.\")\n","\n","DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK = DEV_BLOCKS[0]\n","_dev_view = AUDITOR.guard(\"psi_bin_edges_and_cut_points\", dev_df[[ID_COLUMN]])\n","\n","psi_records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n","lift_records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n","risk_rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n","PSI_EDGES: Dict[str, Optional[np.ndarray]] = {}\n","DECILE_CUT_POINTS: Dict[str, float] = {}\n","\n","for feature in AUDIT_FEATURES:\n","    dev_values = dev_df[feature]\n","    oot_values = oot_df[feature]\n","\n","    # ---- development-only fitted objects: bin edges and the decile cut point\n","    edges = learn_psi_bins(dev_df.loc[dev_df[\"chrono_block\"] == DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK, feature])\n","    PSI_EDGES[feature] = edges\n","    finite_dev = dev_values[pd.to_numeric(dev_values, errors=\"coerce\").map(np.isfinite)]\n","    cut_point = (float(np.quantile(finite_dev, CONFIG[\"TOP_DECILE_QUANTILE\"]))\n","                 if len(finite_dev) >= CONFIG[\"MIN_NON_MISSING\"] else float(\"nan\"))\n","    DECILE_CUT_POINTS[feature] = cut_point\n","    reference_mask = dev_df[\"chrono_block\"] == DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK\n","    reference_ids = dev_df.loc[reference_mask, ID_COLUMN].to_numpy()\n","    AUDITOR.register_fit(f\"psi_edges::{feature}\", \"bin_edges\",\n","                         reference_ids, [DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK])\n","    AUDITOR.register_fit(f\"decile_cut::{feature}\", \"threshold\",\n","                         dev_df[ID_COLUMN].to_numpy(), DEV_BLOCKS)\n","\n","    # ---- PSI: dev reference block vs later dev blocks, then dev vs OOT -------\n","    psi_pairs: Dict[str, float] = {}\n","    for block in DEV_BLOCKS[1:]:\n","        res = calculate_psi(dev_df.loc[dev_df[\"chrono_block\"] == DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK, feature],\n","                            dev_df.loc[dev_df[\"chrono_block\"] == block, feature],\n","                            edges=edges)\n","        psi_pairs[f\"block{DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK}_vs_block{block}\"] = res[\"psi\"]\n","        psi_records.append({\"feature\": feature,\n","                            \"pair\": f\"block{DEV_REFERENCE_BLOCK}_vs_block{block}\",\n","                            \"psi\": res[\"psi\"], \"n_reference\": res[\"n_reference\"],\n","                            \"n_comparison\": res[\"n_comparison\"],\n","                            \"scope\": \"development\"})\n","    res_oot = calculate_psi(dev_values, oot_values, edges=edges)\n","    psi_pairs[f\"dev_vs_block{OOT_BLOCK}\"] = res_oot[\"psi\"]\n","    psi_records.append({\"feature\": feature, \"pair\": f\"dev_vs_block{OOT_BLOCK}\",\n","                        \"psi\": res_oot[\"psi\"], \"n_reference\": res_oot[\"n_reference\"],\n","                        \"n_comparison\": res_oot[\"n_comparison\"],\n","                        \"scope\": \"oot_evaluation_only\"})\n","\n","    finite_psi = {k: v for k, v in psi_pairs.items() if np.isfinite(v)}\n","    dev_finite_psi = {\n","        k: v for k, v in finite_psi.items()\n","        if not k.startswith(\"dev_vs_block\")\n","    }\n","    # Decision summaries are development-only. OOT PSI remains a separate\n","    # evaluation diagnostic and cannot become the maximum or worst pair.\n","    psi_max = max(dev_finite_psi.values()) if dev_finite_psi else np.nan\n","    psi_mean = (float(np.mean(list(dev_finite_psi.values())))\n","                if dev_finite_psi else np.nan)\n","    worst_pair = (max(dev_finite_psi, key=dev_finite_psi.get)\n","                  if dev_finite_psi else \"\")\n","    psi_max_dev = psi_max\n","\n","    # ---- per-block top-decile lift, using the development cut point ---------\n","    block_lifts: Dict[int, float] = {}\n","    for block in DEV_BLOCKS:\n","        block_frame = dev_df.loc[\n","            dev_df[\"chrono_block\"] == block,\n","            [feature, TARGET_COLUMN],\n","        ]\n","        result = calculate_top_decile_lift(block_frame, feature, cut_point)\n","        lift_records.append({\n","            \"feature\": feature,\n","            \"block\": block,\n","            **{k: v for k, v in result.items() if k != \"feature\"},\n","        })\n","        if result[\"assessable\"]:\n","            block_lifts[block] = result[\"lift\"]\n","    \n","    dev_lifts = block_lifts\n","    stability = calculate_lift_stability(dev_lifts)\n","\n","    # ---- missingness drift: dev vs OOT missing-rate difference --------------\n","    dev_missing = float(dev_values.isna().mean())\n","    oot_missing = float(oot_values.isna().mean())\n","\n","    risk_rows.append({\n","        \"feature\": feature,\n","        \"family\": family_of(feature),\n","        \"development_non_missing_count\": int(dev_values.notna().sum()),\n","        \"oot_non_missing_count\": int(oot_values.notna().sum()),\n","        \"PSI_max\": psi_max,\n","        \"PSI_max_development_only\": psi_max_dev,\n","        \"PSI_mean\": psi_mean,\n","        \"PSI_worst_block_pair\": worst_pair,\n","        \"PSI_band_development_only\": classify_psi(psi_max_dev),\n","        \"PSI_dev_vs_oot\": psi_pairs.get(f\"dev_vs_block{OOT_BLOCK}\", np.nan),\n","        \"lift_by_block\": json.dumps({str(k): round(v, 4) for k, v in sorted(block_lifts.items())}),\n","        \"lift_stability\": stability[\"lift_stability\"],\n","        \"lift_stability_blocks\": stability[\"n_blocks\"],\n","        \"lift_mean_development\": stability[\"mean_lift\"],\n","        \"lift_direction\": stability[\"direction\"],\n","        \"development_missing_rate\": round(dev_missing, 6),\n","        \"oot_missing_rate\": round(oot_missing, 6),\n","        \"missingness_drift\": round(oot_missing - dev_missing, 6),\n","    })\n","\n","PSI_LONG = pd.DataFrame(psi_records)\n","LIFT_LONG = pd.DataFrame(lift_records)\n","feature_risk = pd.DataFrame(risk_rows)\n","\n","# --- KS: block 1 vs block 4, both development, with BH correction ------------\n","ks_table = run_ks_tests(dev_df, AUDIT_FEATURES, block_a=DEV_BLOCKS[0], block_b=DEV_BLOCKS[-1])\n","ks_adjusted = adjust_multiple_tests(ks_table[\"ks_pvalue\"].to_numpy())\n","ks_table[\"ks_adjusted_pvalue\"] = ks_adjusted[\"adjusted_pvalue\"].to_numpy()\n","ks_table[\"ks_reject_bh\"] = ks_adjusted[\"reject\"].to_numpy()\n","AUDITOR.register_fit(\"ks_block1_vs_block4\", \"hypothesis_test\",\n","                     dev_df[ID_COLUMN].to_numpy(), DEV_BLOCKS)\n","\n","# --- Spearman association with elapsed time, development rows only -----------\n","spearman_table = calculate_spearman_time_risk(dev_df, AUDIT_FEATURES)\n","spearman_adjusted = adjust_multiple_tests(spearman_table[\"spearman_pvalue\"].to_numpy())\n","spearman_table[\"spearman_adjusted_pvalue\"] = spearman_adjusted[\"adjusted_pvalue\"].to_numpy()\n","AUDITOR.register_fit(\"spearman_time_risk\", \"association_score\",\n","                     dev_df[ID_COLUMN].to_numpy(), DEV_BLOCKS)\n","\n","feature_risk = (feature_risk\n","                .merge(ks_table.rename(columns={\"n_a\": \"ks_n_block1\", \"n_b\": \"ks_n_block4\"})\n","                       [[\"feature\", \"ks_stat\", \"ks_pvalue\", \"ks_adjusted_pvalue\",\n","                         \"ks_reject_bh\", \"ks_n_block1\", \"ks_n_block4\"]],\n","                       on=\"feature\", how=\"left\")\n","                .merge(spearman_table[[\"feature\", \"spearman_corr_time\", \"spearman_pvalue\",\n","                                       \"spearman_adjusted_pvalue\", \"n\"]]\n","                       .rename(columns={\"n\": \"spearman_n\"}),\n","                       on=\"feature\", how=\"left\"))\n","\n","\n","def assign_verdict(row: pd.Series, spearman_cut: float) -> Tuple[str, str, str]:\n","    \"\"\"Map development-only evidence onto (verdict, action, reason).\n","\n","    Only development evidence is consulted: PSI within development blocks, the\n","    dev-only KS comparison, the dev Spearman association and dev lift\n","    stability. The dev-vs-OOT PSI column exists for *reporting* and is\n","    deliberately not read here.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    reasons: List[str] = []\n","    psi_dev = row[\"PSI_max_development_only\"]\n","    if not np.isfinite(psi_dev) and not np.isfinite(row[\"ks_stat\"]):\n","        return (\"insufficient_evidence\", \"investigate\",\n","                \"neither PSI nor KS was assessable (constant, empty or too sparse \"\n","                f\"in a block; dev non-missing = {row['development_non_missing_count']:,})\")\n","\n","    band = classify_psi(psi_dev)\n","    if band == \"severe_drift\":\n","        reasons.append(f\"dev PSI_max {psi_dev:.3f} > {CONFIG['PSI_SEVERE_THRESHOLD']} \"\n","                       f\"(worst pair {row['PSI_worst_block_pair']})\")\n","    elif band == \"moderate_drift\":\n","        reasons.append(f\"dev PSI_max {psi_dev:.3f} in the configured moderate band\")\n","\n","    strong_time = np.isfinite(row[\"spearman_corr_time\"]) and abs(row[\"spearman_corr_time\"]) >= spearman_cut\n","    if strong_time:\n","        reasons.append(f\"|Spearman(feature, elapsed time)| = \"\n","                       f\"{abs(row['spearman_corr_time']):.3f} >= {spearman_cut:.3f} \"\n","                       f\"(BH-adjusted p = {row['spearman_adjusted_pvalue']:.3g})\")\n","\n","    unstable_lift = (row[\"lift_stability\"] is not None\n","                     and np.isfinite(row[\"lift_stability\"] if row[\"lift_stability\"] is not None else np.nan)\n","                     and row[\"lift_stability\"] < CONFIG[\"LIFT_STABILITY_THRESHOLD\"])\n","    if unstable_lift:\n","        reasons.append(f\"top-decile lift stability {row['lift_stability']:.2f} < \"\n","                       f\"{CONFIG['LIFT_STABILITY_THRESHOLD']:.2f} \"\n","                       f\"across {int(row['lift_stability_blocks'])} dev blocks\")\n","    if row[\"lift_stability\"] is None:\n","        reasons.append(\"lift stability not estimable (too few blocks with enough positives)\")\n","\n","\n","    if band == \"severe_drift\" or (strong_time and unstable_lift):\n","        return (\"temporal_risk\", \"tag_not_drop\", \"; \".join(reasons))\n","    if band == \"moderate_drift\" or strong_time or unstable_lift:\n","        return (\"moderate_risk\", \"monitor\", \"; \".join(reasons))\n","    if not np.isfinite(psi_dev):\n","        return (\n","            \"insufficient_evidence\",\n","            \"investigate\",\n","            \"development PSI is unassessable and no configured non-PSI risk rule triggered\",\n","        )\n","    return (\"stable\", \"keep\",\n","            f\"dev PSI_max {psi_dev:.3f} below {CONFIG['PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD']}, \"\n","            f\"|Spearman| {abs(row['spearman_corr_time']):.3f} below {spearman_cut:.3f}\"\n","            if np.isfinite(row[\"spearman_corr_time\"])\n","            else f\"dev PSI_max {psi_dev:.3f} below {CONFIG['PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD']}; \"\n","                 \"time correlation unassessable\")\n","\n","\n","_verdicts = feature_risk.apply(\n","    lambda r: assign_verdict(r, CONFIG[\"SPEARMAN_RISK_THRESHOLD\"]), axis=1)\n","feature_risk[\"verdict\"] = [v[0] for v in _verdicts]\n","feature_risk[\"action\"] = [v[1] for v in _verdicts]\n","feature_risk[\"reason\"] = [v[2] for v in _verdicts]\n","feature_risk[\"decision_scope\"] = \"development_only\"\n","\n","feature_risk = feature_risk.sort_values([\"family\", \"feature\"], kind=\"mergesort\").reset_index(drop=True)\n","FEATURE_RISK_PATH = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIRECTORY, \"feature_risk_table.csv\")\n","feature_risk.to_csv(FEATURE_RISK_PATH, index=False)\n","LOG.info(\"Wrote %s (%d features x %d columns).\", FEATURE_RISK_PATH, *feature_risk.shape)\n","\n","print(feature_risk.groupby([\"family\", \"verdict\"]).size().rename(\"features\").reset_index().to_string(index=False))\n","print(\"\\nD-series detail (the family the source notebook flagged as range-expanding):\")\n","_d_view = feature_risk[feature_risk.family == \"D\"][\n","    [\"feature\", \"development_non_missing_count\", \"PSI_max_development_only\",\n","     \"ks_stat\", \"ks_adjusted_pvalue\", \"spearman_corr_time\", \"lift_stability\",\n","     \"missingness_drift\", \"verdict\", \"action\"]]\n","print(_d_view.to_string(index=False))\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 3.6))\n","_plot = feature_risk.dropna(subset=[\"PSI_max_development_only\"])\n","axes[0].hist(_plot[\"PSI_max_development_only\"], bins=40)\n","axes[0].axvline(CONFIG[\"PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD\"], color=\"orange\", ls=\"--\",\n","                label=f\"moderate {CONFIG['PSI_MODERATE_THRESHOLD']}\")\n","axes[0].axvline(CONFIG[\"PSI_SEVERE_THRESHOLD\"], color=\"crimson\", ls=\"--\",\n","                label=f\"severe {CONFIG['PSI_SEVERE_THRESHOLD']}\")\n","axes[0].set_xlabel(\"max PSI across development block pairs\")\n","axes[0].set_ylabel(\"features\")\n","axes[0].set_title(\"Development PSI distribution (configured bands shown)\")\n","axes[0].legend(fontsize=8)\n","axes[1].scatter(feature_risk[\"spearman_corr_time\"].abs(),\n","                feature_risk[\"PSI_max_development_only\"], s=10, alpha=0.5)\n","axes[1].set_xlabel(\"|Spearman correlation with elapsed time| (development)\")\n","axes[1].set_ylabel(\"max development PSI\")\n","axes[1].set_title(\"Two independent views of temporal risk\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b17468f0","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"28642064-69f0-47da-b2ef-7c8e0e4c84aa","_uuid":"793dcf93-a38a-49a4-89cc-968cf887765a","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.014307,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.924815+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.910508+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Interpreting Section 5\n","\n","Three points a reader should hold onto:\n","\n","1. **The verdict rule reads development evidence only.** `PSI_dev_vs_oot` is\n","   computed and exported because RQ7 asks about OOT generalization risk, but\n","   `assign_verdict` never reads it. That separation is the difference between\n","   *reporting* on the holdout and *deciding* with it.\n","2. **A tiny KS p-value is not a finding.** With ~120,000 rows per block, KS\n","   detects differences far below anything that would change a model's behaviour.\n","   The statistic (a maximum CDF gap) is the effect size; the adjusted p-value\n","   only says the gap is not sampling noise.\n","3. **Lift stability is withheld, not defaulted.** A feature whose top decile\n","   contains fewer than the configured minimum positives returns\n","   `insufficient_evidence`, which propagates into the ledger as `null` rather\n","   than as a flattering number."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7369ca01","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"476f9fad-eda3-4d8c-9b7e-015d648c6662","_uuid":"c046f0ea-3efb-4893-8b61-2400442e1a07","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.014083,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.953527+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.939444+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 6. Missingness Stability and Confounding\n","\n","Columns blank on exactly the same rows are collapsed into one **missingness\n","pattern** before testing. Without this, a single underlying event — most often\n","\"the identity table had no matching row\" — is counted once per column, inflating\n","both the discovery count and the multiplicity correction.\n","\n","Each pattern then gets: a missing rate by block, fraud rates for the missing and\n","observed groups by block with their positive counts, a ProductCD-stratified\n","repeat of the same contrast, a chi-square test with BH correction, a\n","direction-consistency requirement across development blocks, and an explicit\n","check for sign reversal inside strata."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"5c6046a4","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"46e97963-d179-4eae-a3cb-3065868347c5","_uuid":"f78878bc-94a4-47df-9183-8a90f22cd808","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.984747Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.984436Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.137898Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.137045Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":16.171677,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.13974+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:23.968063+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["09:17:26 | INFO    | 339 partially-missing columns collapse to 65 distinct missingness patterns.\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Patterns tested: 65 of 65; surviving BH + effect size + direction consistency: 27.\n","Patterns whose aggregate direction reverses inside at least one reliable ProductCD stratum: 32. A reversal is a Simpson-type warning: the aggregate association is at least partly a product-mix effect. This is an association, not evidence that blankness causes fraud.\n","\n","Top patterns by |effect size|:\n"," pattern_lead  n_columns  n_blank  n_filled  delta_pp    phi  adjusted_pvalue  direction_consistency  keep_indicator\n","           D7          1   442488     29944   -12.230 0.1618              0.0                    1.0           False\n","        addr1          2    53761    418671     8.898 0.1534              0.0                    1.0            True\n","          D14          1   422596     49836    -8.885 0.1482              0.0                    1.0           False\n","          D12          1   419729     52703    -8.844 0.1512              0.0                    1.0            True\n","          D13          1   423459     48973    -8.193 0.1356              0.0                    1.0           False\n","        id_03          2   418342     54090    -7.818 0.1352              0.0                    1.0           False\n","           D6          1   413949     58483    -7.759 0.1388              0.0                    1.0           False\n","           D8          4   410822     61610    -7.620 0.1393              0.0                    1.0            True\n","        dist2          1   440332     32100    -6.401 0.0875              0.0                    1.0           False\n","        id_13          1   367262    105170    -5.821 0.1315              0.0                    1.0           False\n","R_emaildomain          1   358812    113620    -5.818 0.1350              0.0                    1.0           False\n","        id_05          2   357945    114487    -5.580 0.1299              0.0                    1.0            True\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1430x440 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1100x396 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["\"\"\"Section 6 - missingness stability, ProductCD stratification and confounding.\"\"\"\n","\n","\n","def analyze_missingness_by_block(frame: pd.DataFrame, features: Sequence[str],\n","                                 target: str = TARGET_COLUMN,\n","                                 block_column: str = \"chrono_block\",\n","                                 min_group_n: int = CONFIG[\"MIN_GROUP_N\"]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Missing rate and fraud rate for the missing vs observed group, per block.\n","\n","    Every returned rate carries its own denominator (``n_missing`` /\n","    ``n_observed``) so no percentage in the output is unattributable. Groups\n","    smaller than ``min_group_n`` are reported with ``reliable = False`` rather\n","    than dropped, because their absence would itself be informative.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if not features:\n","        raise ValueError(\"analyze_missingness_by_block requires at least one feature.\")\n","    rows = []\n","    for feature in features:\n","        indicator = frame[feature].isna()\n","        for block, idx in frame.groupby(block_column).groups.items():\n","            sub_missing = indicator.loc[idx]\n","            y = frame.loc[idx, target]\n","            n_missing, n_observed = int(sub_missing.sum()), int((~sub_missing).sum())\n","            rows.append({\n","                \"feature\": feature, \"block\": int(block),\n","                \"n\": len(idx), \"n_missing\": n_missing, \"n_observed\": n_observed,\n","                \"missing_rate\": n_missing / len(idx) if len(idx) else np.nan,\n","                \"positives_missing\": int(y[sub_missing].sum()),\n","                \"positives_observed\": int(y[~sub_missing].sum()),\n","                \"fraud_rate_missing\": float(y[sub_missing].mean()) if n_missing else np.nan,\n","                \"fraud_rate_observed\": float(y[~sub_missing].mean()) if n_observed else np.nan,\n","                \"reliable\": min(n_missing, n_observed) >= min_group_n,\n","            })\n","    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","    out[\"delta_pp\"] = 100 * (out[\"fraud_rate_missing\"] - out[\"fraud_rate_observed\"])\n","    return out\n","\n","\n","def analyze_missingness_by_product(frame: pd.DataFrame, features: Sequence[str],\n","                                   product_column: str = \"ProductCD\",\n","                                   target: str = TARGET_COLUMN,\n","                                   min_group_n: int = CONFIG[\"MIN_GROUP_N\"]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Same contrast as ``analyze_missingness_by_block`` but stratified by product.\n","\n","    The aggregate \"missing implies more/less fraud\" relationship can invert\n","    inside a stratum when ProductCD drives both the missingness and the fraud\n","    rate. This function produces the per-stratum evidence needed to check that,\n","    and the caller compares the signs.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if product_column not in frame.columns:\n","        raise KeyError(f\"'{product_column}' is not present; stratified analysis \"\n","                       \"cannot run and must be recorded as not computed.\")\n","    rows = []\n","    for feature in features:\n","        indicator = frame[feature].isna()\n","        for product, idx in frame.groupby(product_column, observed=True).groups.items():\n","            sub_missing = indicator.loc[idx]\n","            y = frame.loc[idx, target]\n","            n_missing, n_observed = int(sub_missing.sum()), int((~sub_missing).sum())\n","            rows.append({\n","                \"feature\": feature, \"product\": product, \"n\": len(idx),\n","                \"n_missing\": n_missing, \"n_observed\": n_observed,\n","                \"positives_missing\": int(y[sub_missing].sum()),\n","                \"positives_observed\": int(y[~sub_missing].sum()),\n","                \"fraud_rate_missing\": float(y[sub_missing].mean()) if n_missing else np.nan,\n","                \"fraud_rate_observed\": float(y[~sub_missing].mean()) if n_observed else np.nan,\n","                \"reliable\": min(n_missing, n_observed) >= min_group_n,\n","            })\n","    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n","    out[\"delta_pp\"] = 100 * (out[\"fraud_rate_missing\"] - out[\"fraud_rate_observed\"])\n","    return out\n","\n","\n","def group_by_missingness_pattern(frame: pd.DataFrame, features: Sequence[str]) -> Dict[str, List[str]]:\n","    \"\"\"Collapse columns that are blank on exactly the same rows into one pattern.\n","\n","    Testing each column separately would count one underlying signal (for\n","    example \"the identity table had no matching row\") once per column and\n","    inflate both the discovery count and the multiplicity correction. Hashing\n","    the boolean missing-mask is O(n) per column instead of O(n) per pair.\n","    Representative = the first column in deterministic sorted order.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    buckets: Dict[Any, List[str]] = {}\n","    for column in features:\n","        key = hashlib.sha1(frame[column].isna().to_numpy().tobytes()).hexdigest()\n","        buckets.setdefault(key, []).append(column)\n","    return {sorted(members)[0]: sorted(members) for members in buckets.values()}\n","\n","\n","# --- candidate features: those with genuinely partial missingness in dev -----\n","_missing_rate_dev = dev_df[FEATURE_COLUMNS].isna().mean()\n","MISSINGNESS_CANDIDATES = sorted(_missing_rate_dev[(_missing_rate_dev > CONFIG[\"PARTIAL_MISSING_MIN_RATE\"])\n","                                                  & (_missing_rate_dev < CONFIG[\"PARTIAL_MISSING_MAX_RATE\"])].index)\n","PATTERN_GROUPS = group_by_missingness_pattern(dev_df, MISSINGNESS_CANDIDATES)\n","PATTERN_LEADS = sorted(PATTERN_GROUPS)\n","LOG.info(\"%d partially-missing columns collapse to %d distinct missingness patterns.\",\n","         len(MISSINGNESS_CANDIDATES), len(PATTERN_LEADS))\n","\n","AUDITOR.guard(\"missingness_pattern_tests\", dev_df[[ID_COLUMN]])\n","MISSING_BY_BLOCK = analyze_missingness_by_block(dev_df, PATTERN_LEADS)\n","MISSING_BY_PRODUCT = analyze_missingness_by_product(dev_df, PATTERN_LEADS)\n","\n","# --- one chi-square test per PATTERN, on development rows, BH-corrected -----\n","_rows = []\n","_y_dev = dev_df[TARGET_COLUMN]\n","for lead in PATTERN_LEADS:\n","    blank = dev_df[lead].isna()\n","    n_blank, n_filled = int(blank.sum()), int((~blank).sum())\n","    if min(n_blank, n_filled) < CONFIG[\"MIN_GROUP_N\"]:\n","        _rows.append({\"pattern_lead\": lead, \"n_columns\": len(PATTERN_GROUPS[lead]),\n","                      \"n_blank\": n_blank, \"n_filled\": n_filled, \"delta_pp\": np.nan,\n","                      \"phi\": np.nan, \"pvalue\": np.nan, \"tested\": False,\n","                      \"reason\": f\"a group has fewer than {CONFIG['MIN_GROUP_N']} rows\"})\n","        continue\n","    k_blank, k_filled = int(_y_dev[blank].sum()), int(_y_dev[~blank].sum())\n","    table = np.array([[k_blank, n_blank - k_blank], [k_filled, n_filled - k_filled]])\n","    chi2, pvalue, _, _ = stats.chi2_contingency(table)\n","    delta_pp = 100 * (k_blank / n_blank - k_filled / n_filled)\n","    # Per-block sign consistency within development.\n","    signs = []\n","    for block in DEV_BLOCKS:\n","        m = dev_df[\"chrono_block\"] == block\n","        if (blank & m).sum() >= CONFIG[\"MIN_BLOCK_GROUP_N\"] and ((~blank) & m).sum() >= CONFIG[\"MIN_BLOCK_GROUP_N\"]:\n","            signs.append(np.sign(_y_dev[blank & m].mean() - _y_dev[(~blank) & m].mean()))\n","    consistency = float(np.mean(np.array(signs) == np.sign(delta_pp))) if signs else np.nan\n","    _rows.append({\"pattern_lead\": lead, \"n_columns\": len(PATTERN_GROUPS[lead]),\n","                  \"n_blank\": n_blank, \"n_filled\": n_filled,\n","                  \"delta_pp\": round(delta_pp, 3),\n","                  \"phi\": round(float(np.sqrt(chi2 / len(_y_dev))), 4),\n","                  \"pvalue\": float(pvalue), \"direction_consistency\": consistency,\n","                  \"tested\": True, \"reason\": \"\"})\n","\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS = pd.DataFrame(_rows)\n","_adj = adjust_multiple_tests(MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"pvalue\"].to_numpy())\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"adjusted_pvalue\"] = _adj[\"adjusted_pvalue\"].to_numpy()\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"reject_bh\"] = _adj[\"reject\"].to_numpy()\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator\"] = (\n","    MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"reject_bh\"]\n","    & (MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"delta_pp\"].abs() >= CONFIG[\"MIN_ABS_DELTA_PP\"])\n","    & (MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"direction_consistency\"] >= 0.75)\n",")\n","\n","# --- Simpson / confounding check against ProductCD --------------------------\n","_conf_rows = []\n","for lead in PATTERN_LEADS:\n","    aggregate = MISSINGNESS_TESTS.loc[MISSINGNESS_TESTS.pattern_lead == lead, \"delta_pp\"]\n","    if aggregate.empty or not np.isfinite(aggregate.iloc[0]):\n","        continue\n","    agg_sign = np.sign(aggregate.iloc[0])\n","    strata = MISSING_BY_PRODUCT[(MISSING_BY_PRODUCT.feature == lead)\n","                                & MISSING_BY_PRODUCT.reliable\n","                                & MISSING_BY_PRODUCT.delta_pp.notna()]\n","    if strata.empty:\n","        _conf_rows.append({\"pattern_lead\": lead, \"n_reliable_strata\": 0,\n","                           \"share_agreeing\": np.nan, \"flag\": \"no_reliable_strata\"})\n","        continue\n","    agree = float((np.sign(strata.delta_pp) == agg_sign).mean())\n","    _conf_rows.append({\n","        \"pattern_lead\": lead, \"n_reliable_strata\": int(len(strata)),\n","        \"share_agreeing\": round(agree, 3),\n","        \"flag\": (\"sign_reverses_in_some_strata\" if agree < 1.0 else \"consistent\"),\n","    })\n","CONFOUNDING = pd.DataFrame(_conf_rows)\n","_reversal_by_lead = (CONFOUNDING.set_index(\"pattern_lead\")[\"flag\"].to_dict()\n","                     if len(CONFOUNDING) else {})\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"productcd_reversal_flag\"] = MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"pattern_lead\"].map(\n","    lambda lead: _reversal_by_lead.get(lead, \"not_assessed\")\n",")\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator_pre_reversal\"] = MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator\"]\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator\"] = (\n","    MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator_pre_reversal\"]\n","    & MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"productcd_reversal_flag\"].eq(\"consistent\")\n",")\n","MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"indicator_action\"] = np.where(\n","    MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator\"],\n","    \"keep_indicator\",\n","    np.where(\n","        MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"keep_indicator_pre_reversal\"]\n","        & MISSINGNESS_TESTS[\"productcd_reversal_flag\"].ne(\"consistent\"),\n","        \"investigate_product_mix\",\n","        \"do_not_keep\",\n","    ),\n",")\n","\n","_reversals = CONFOUNDING[CONFOUNDING.flag == \"sign_reverses_in_some_strata\"]\n","print(f\"Patterns tested: {int(MISSINGNESS_TESTS.tested.sum())} of {len(MISSINGNESS_TESTS)}; \"\n","      f\"surviving BH + effect size + direction consistency: \"\n","      f\"{int(MISSINGNESS_TESTS.keep_indicator.sum())}.\")\n","print(f\"Patterns whose aggregate direction reverses inside at least one reliable \"\n","      f\"ProductCD stratum: {len(_reversals)}. A reversal is a Simpson-type warning: \"\n","      \"the aggregate association is at least partly a product-mix effect. This is an \"\n","      \"association, not evidence that blankness causes fraud.\")\n","print(\"\\nTop patterns by |effect size|:\")\n","print(MISSINGNESS_TESTS.reindex(MISSINGNESS_TESTS.delta_pp.abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index)\n","      .head(12)[[\"pattern_lead\", \"n_columns\", \"n_blank\", \"n_filled\", \"delta_pp\",\n","                 \"phi\", \"adjusted_pvalue\", \"direction_consistency\", \"keep_indicator\"]]\n","      .to_string(index=False))\n","\n","_top = (MISSINGNESS_TESTS.reindex(MISSINGNESS_TESTS.delta_pp.abs()\n","                                  .sort_values(ascending=False).index)\n","        .head(6)[\"pattern_lead\"].tolist())\n","if _top:\n","    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\n","    for lead in _top:\n","        series = MISSING_BY_BLOCK[MISSING_BY_BLOCK.feature == lead]\n","        axes[0].plot(series.block, 100 * series.missing_rate, marker=\"o\", label=lead)\n","        axes[1].plot(series.block, series.delta_pp, marker=\"o\", label=lead)\n","    axes[0].set_xlabel(\"development block\")\n","    axes[0].set_ylabel(\"missing rate (%)\")\n","    axes[0].set_title(\"Missingness rate by block (development only)\")\n","    axes[1].axhline(0, color=\"grey\", lw=1)\n","    axes[1].set_xlabel(\"development block\")\n","    axes[1].set_ylabel(\"fraud rate: missing minus observed (pp)\")\n","    axes[1].set_title(\"Is the missingness signal stable over time?\")\n","    for ax in axes:\n","        ax.set_xticks(DEV_BLOCKS)\n","        ax.legend(fontsize=7, ncol=2)\n","    plt.tight_layout()\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","    _strata = MISSING_BY_PRODUCT[MISSING_BY_PRODUCT.feature.isin(_top)\n","                                 & MISSING_BY_PRODUCT.reliable]\n","    if not _strata.empty:\n","        fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 3.6))\n","        for lead, part in _strata.groupby(\"feature\"):\n","            ax.scatter(part[\"product\"].astype(str), part.delta_pp, label=lead, s=45)\n","        ax.axhline(0, color=\"grey\", lw=1)\n","        ax.set_xlabel(\"ProductCD stratum\")\n","        ax.set_ylabel(\"fraud rate: missing minus observed (pp)\")\n","        ax.set_title(\"Missingness effect within ProductCD strata \"\n","                     \"(points below zero reverse the usual aggregate direction)\")\n","        ax.legend(fontsize=7, ncol=3)\n","        plt.tight_layout()\n","        plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bba9bda5","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"6784c4f3-e6a3-410b-9a19-eaf08515b89a","_uuid":"669c96b0-da93-4da2-ba76-d9bd935980ca","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.016406,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.173595+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.157189+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Interpreting Section 6\n","\n","A **sign reversal inside a ProductCD stratum is a Simpson-type warning**: the\n","aggregate contrast is at least partly a product-mix effect, because ProductCD\n","drives both the availability of the field and the base fraud rate. The\n","stratified panel is what separates the two; the aggregate number alone cannot.\n","\n","A negative gap — blank implies *less* fraud — is usually the join, not the\n","customer. Before any such indicator is carried into a model it must be checked\n","against the identity-table coverage, because \"no identity record existed\" is a\n","data-collection fact, not a behavioural one.\n","\n","Nothing in this section supports a causal reading. Missingness is associated with\n","the outcome; that is the entire claim."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6d474059","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"5592f261-543e-43a4-aedb-f90ca4dfc443","_uuid":"558d7300-f6b4-4475-83ba-fccf4a8e1317","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.016123,"end_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.206158+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.190035+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 7. V-Series Redundancy and Stability\n","\n","Development data only, in eight deterministic steps: per-block Spearman\n","correlation → distance `1 − |ρ|` → average-linkage hierarchical clustering →\n","cross-block co-membership → retain only clusters stable across development blocks\n","→ pick one representative per stable cluster by mutual information with the\n","target on development rows → deterministic tie-breaking (MI, then completeness,\n","then name) → record why each representative won.\n","\n","**Approximation, labelled as such:** each block's correlation matrix is estimated\n","on an evenly-spaced sample of that block when it exceeds the configured row\n","budget. Evenly spaced rather than random keeps the within-block chronology and\n","keeps the result reproducible without a seed. The sampling note is printed per\n","block and stored with the run.\n","\n","No reducer is fitted. Deciding what *could* be reduced is EDA; performing the\n","reduction is modelling, and a reducer fitted here would have to be refitted\n","inside each training fold anyway to stay leakage-safe."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"84d131d7","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"07315d49-6ec2-46ae-b4e7-3566176fd6fb","_uuid":"1321dedd-d9e1-49a2-a2fc-e3ba298f69cc","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.241303Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-29T09:17:40.24097Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-29T09:25:17.934473Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-29T09:25:17.933488Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"pap